{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HomwPUwHcQCwixKNA2erZ9","type":"tool_result","content":"259:- `game.screen.ctx`: its 2D context (r.ctx is the same)\n417:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the mus\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n----\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under \n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n946:- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n957:- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase).\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"5e8826c4-a567-421d-bbc7-66fae603bd65","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:42.008Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"259:- `game.screen.ctx`: its 2D context (r.ctx is the same)\n417:- `r.ctx`: the low-resolution buffer's 2D context: draw on it with E.px\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the mus\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n----\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080', alpha: .3, rays }. Call it in draw (it is a decal: under \n941:- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n942:- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n946:- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n957:- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n965:- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n1002:- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase).\n1003:- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n1005:- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n1014:- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HomwPUwHcQCwixKNA2erZ9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyrtaCVX9g6mgEEhRqM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HZB6s7M7Nx6KTnsvUMkTtK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/plan-xb43d63-research/engine/repo/dist/handoff && sed -n '935,1016p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420","description":"Read the Mover, actions and perception index entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3159,"cache_read_input_tokens":246650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3159},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"a3fdb3fb-7abd-4855-b810-843db309e548","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:45.540Z","request_id":"req_011CggyrtK4yVDJvBYeJHLGS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HZB6s7M7Nx6KTnsvUMkTtK":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/plan-xb43d63-research/engine/repo/dist/handoff && sed -n '935,1016p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-420","description":"Read the Mover, actions and perception index entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZB6s7M7Nx6KTnsvUMkTtK","type":"tool_result","content":"- `body.step = 2`: the height it walks up without jumping (E.HEIGHTS.step)\n- `body.vx = 0`, `body.vy = 0`, `body.vz = 0`: its speed, world units per second\n- `body.x = 0`, `body.y = 0`, `body.z = 0`: its position (z = feet)\n\n## 17b. Actions\n\n- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n- `action.canCancel` †: true during a beat marked as one the action may be cut short in (spec.cancel)\n- `action.cancel()` †: stop now: the bodies stay where they are\n- `action.invulnerable` †: true while hits should miss (spec.safe: [from, to] of the action's progress)\n- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n- `action.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state for the body (merge extra over it): x, y, z, its speed, facing and the beat's pose\n- `action.u` †: 0..1 through the whole action\n- `action.update(dt)` †: move the bodies one step; returns true while the action runs (false once it has ended)\n- `action.beat` †: the name of the beat playing now\n- `action.beats` †: [[name, seconds], ...]\n- `action.body`, `action.other` †: the bodies it moves\n- `action.done = false` †: it has ended (or was cancelled)\n- `action.duration` †: the action's length in seconds (o.speed shortens it)\n- `action.name` †: the action's name\n- `action.o` †: the options it was given\n- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n- `action.start` †: where the body was when it began\n- `action.t = 0` †: seconds played\n\n## 17c. Mover\n\n- `new E.Mover(o = {}) → mover`: new E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, ... }): any of its fields, below, as options. An E.Body: it has body.jump, push and the body's fields too\n- `mover.dodge(dir, dist = 34)` †: a dodge roll toward dir (an angle or [dx, dy]; default its facing) when it stands free. Returns the action, or null\n- `mover.play(name, o = {})` †: start an action now (E.ACTIONS name, its options): it moves the body until it ends\n- `mover.respawn()` †: back to the last safe spot (after water, a pit, a fall it shouldn't survive)\n- `mover.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state: rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({ attack })): its motion, crouch, sprint and landing, or the playing action's pose; extra is merged over it\n- `mover.update(dt, map, ctl = {}, view)` †: one step. ctl: game.input (needs the actions move, jump, and sprint / crouch if it has them; screen directions turn into ground ones through view, the game's by default) or an intent { move: [dx, dy], sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }\n- `mover.accel = 700`, `mover.airAccel = 260` †: how fast it gets there\n- `mover.action = null` †: the E.Action playing, or null\n- `mover.buffer = .12` †: seconds a jump press is kept\n- `mover.climb = true` †: climbs ledges (true)\n- `mover.climbAny = false` †: climbs any wall face (see the section's header)\n- `mover.climbMax = 82` †: the highest ledge it climbs\n- `mover.climbSpeed = 34` †: its climbing speed\n- `mover.coyote = .1` †: seconds a jump still works after leaving an edge\n- `mover.crouch = false` †: sneaking (a toggle)\n- `mover.exhausted = false` †: out of stamina until a third is back\n- `mover.facing = 0` †: the angle it faces\n- `mover.fell = 0`, `mover.hurt = false`, `mover.inHazard = false` †: what happened this step\n- `mover.gapAssist = true` †: a jump at a gap aims for the far side\n- `mover.glide = false` †: opens a glide in the air (see the header)\n- `mover.glideMin = 24`, `mover.glideSink = 26`, `mover.glideSpeed = 72` †: how high over the ground it opens, how fast it sinks and flies\n- `mover.gliding = false` †: gliding now\n- `mover.hopMax = 48` †: drops up to this deep are hopped down\n- `mover.hurtAt = 72`, `mover.rollAt = 26` †: fall heights that roll and that hurt\n- `mover.jumpSpeed = 220` †: a jump's upward speed\n- `mover.lastSafe = null` †: the last spot it stood safely, for respawn()\n- `mover.lift = 0` †: an updraft's rising speed (a number, or a function of the mover)\n- `mover.run = 85`, `mover.sneak = 32`, `mover.sprintSpeed = 125`, `mover.walk = 50` †: top speeds (world units a second)\n- `mover.sprinting = false` †: sprinting now\n- `mover.stamina` †: what is left (full to start)\n- `mover.staminaMax = 0` †: its stamina (0: none)\n- `mover.staminaRegen = 35` †: refilled a second standing\n- `mover.tire` †: { climb, climbJump, glide, sprint } it costs\n- `mover.turn = 14` †: how fast it turns, radians a second\n- `mover.vault = 14` †: walls up to this high are vaulted at a run\n- `mover.wall = null` †: the face it holds on to (map.wall's), or null\n\n## 17d. Perception\n\n- `new E.Suspicion(o = {}) → suspicion`: new E.Suspicion({ rise, decay, notice, search, alert, forget }): a guard's mind (its fields, below, are its options). Its level rises while it sees the target (faster the more exposed and nearer), decays while it doesn't, and names a state: 'calm', 'notice' (turn and look), 'search' (go to last), 'alert' (chase). An alert guard that loses the target searches for forget seconds\n- `suspicion.hear(strength, at)` †: a noise heard (strength 0..1, from E.hears) at a point: at least noticed, never more than searching\n- `suspicion.reset()` †: back to calm\n- `suspicion.update(dt, seen, target)` †: one step: seen is E.sees' result (or true / false), target the body seen. Returns the state\n- `suspicion.alert = 1`, `suspicion.notice = .3`, `suspicion.search = .65` †: the levels where each state starts\n- `suspicion.changed = false` †: the state changed this step\n- `suspicion.decay = .3`, `suspicion.rise = 1.5` †: per second\n- `suspicion.forget = 6` †: seconds an alert guard searches after losing the target\n- `suspicion.last = null` †: where it last saw or heard the target ({ x, y, z }), or null\n- `suspicion.level = 0` †: 0..1.2, how suspicious\n- `suspicion.since = 0` †: seconds since it last saw or heard anything\n- `suspicion.state = 'calm'` †: 'calm' | 'notice' | 'search' | 'alert'\n- `E.hears(lis, noise, map)`: how loud a noise ({ x, y, z, loud: its radius in world units, 80 }) is where listener stands: 1 at the noise, 0 at its radius and beyond, halved when a top of map stands between them (a wall muffles it)\n- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest, its head) that the observer's eyes see past every top of o.map, times the target's own exposure (default 1) and .6 when it c\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"2f78ee7e-27c2-4692-9b30-d38276514543","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:45.554Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `body.step = 2`: the height it walks up without jumping (E.HEIGHTS.step)\n- `body.vx = 0`, `body.vy = 0`, `body.vz = 0`: its speed, world units per second\n- `body.x = 0`, `body.y = 0`, `body.z = 0`: its position (z = feet)\n\n## 17b. Actions\n\n- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.na