{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggyv8ZevFLkCxBo1KDaA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JcufsyGwvNfUo6Mofwb72g","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/plan-xb43d63-research/engine/repo/dist/handoff && grep -n \"createGain()\" my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-220 | head -12; sed -n '1050,1080p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-240","description":"Find gain nodes and the audio API entries"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":546,"cache_read_input_tokens":264633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":546},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"18df087a-12d9-4817-a8f4-b02def9033c3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:29.689Z","request_id":"req_011Cggyv8K2dh1KB534o9md7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JcufsyGwvNfUo6Mofwb72g":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/plan-xb43d63-research/engine/repo/dist/handoff && grep -n \"createGain()\" my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-220 | head -12; sed -n '1050,1080p' API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-240","description":"Find gain nodes and the audio API entries"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JcufsyGwvNfUo6Mofwb72g","type":"tool_result","content":"7555:      this._master = c.createGain(); this._master.connect(c.destination);\n7556:      this._sfxBus = c.createGain(); this._sfxBus.connect(this._master);\n7557:      this._musBus = c.createGain(); this._musBus.connect(this._master);\n7589:    const g = c.createGain(); g.gain.setValueAtTime(0, t); g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol, t + att);\n7604:      if (p.vib) { const lfo = c.createOscillator(), lg = c.createGain(); lfo.frequency.value = p.vib[0]; lg.gain.value = f0 * p.vib[1]; lfo.connect(lg); lg.connect(src.frequency); lfo.start(t); lfo.stop(end + .05);\n7739:    const c = this.ctx, bus = c.createGain(); bus.connect(this._musBus); C.bus = bus;\n7741:    for (const t of C.tracks) { t.gain = c.createGain(); t.gain.gain.value = C.vols[t.i]; t.gain.connect(bus); }\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is \n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . \n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each tr\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step \n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"7876a2ac-4ef4-423a-a66a-a5f8c969ca4e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:29.710Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"7555:      this._master = c.createGain(); this._master.connect(c.destination);\n7556:      this._sfxBus = c.createGain(); this._sfxBus.connect(this._master);\n7557:      this._musBus = c.createGain(); this._musBus.connect(this._master);\n7589:    const g = c.createGain(); g.gain.setValueAtTime(0, t); g.gain.linearRampToValueAtTime(vol, t + att);\n7604:      if (p.vib) { const lfo = c.createOscillator(), lg = c.createGain(); lfo.frequency.value = p.vib[0]; lg.gain.value = f0 * p.vib[1]; lfo.connect(lg); lg.connect(src.frequency); lfo.start(t); lfo.stop(end + .05);\n7739:    const c = this.ctx, bus = c.createGain(); bus.connect(this._musBus); C.bus = bus;\n7741:    for (const t of C.tracks) { t.gain = c.createGain(); t.gain.gain.value = C.vols[t.i]; t.gain.connect(bus); }\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is \n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . \n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each tr\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step \n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JcufsyGwvNfUo6Mofwb72g","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
