{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2G8ZwgXArLwCnsNpr4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QtVj8QB34RsCQq2mGJ5d15","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10498,"cache_read_input_tokens":460538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10498},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"a05f119a-bd43-4781-bb2b-79eca78cd320","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:15.076Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2G8JKNgoYZmv9HJGds","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QtVj8QB34RsCQq2mGJ5d15":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QtVj8QB34RsCQq2mGJ5d15","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t### 3.6 Data formats (the campaign and the Workshop share them exactly)\n301\t\n302\t**Level** (`def('level', id, spec)`; the Workshop exports the same JSON):\n303\t\n304\t```js\n305\t{ id: 'm1', name: 'Rice and Ash', size: [56, 48], time: 'night' /* dusk | night | rain | festival */, ambient: .38,\n306\t  rows: ['########…', …],                 // terrain only, default legend below (48 strings of 56 chars)\n307\t  zones: [{ id: 'mansion', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], name: 'Kanemori Mansion' }],   // HUD place names\n308\t  lights: [{ at: [cx, cy], z: 18, r: 64, i: .9, color: '#ffb060', kind: 'stoneLantern' }],   // kind also places its prop\n309\t  props: [['stoneLantern', cx, cy, { facing: 0 }], ['bamboo', cx, cy], …],   // solid unless { solid: false }\n310\t  anchors: [[cx, cy, z]],                // extra grapple anchors (tree crowns, beams); roof edges are found automatically\n311\t  hero: { at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 0 }, exit: { at: [cx, cy], r: 1.5 },\n312\t  guards: [{ id: 'g1', type: 'ashigaru', at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 90, mode: 'patrol', lantern: true,\n313\t             route: [[cx, cy, wait, lookDeg], …], loop: true, partner: null, faction: 'kanemori' }],\n314\t  civilians: [{ id: 'c1', type: 'maid', at: [cx, cy], mode: 'idle', route: null, disguised: false }],\n315\t  pickups: [{ id: 'ledger', kind: 'story', at: [cx, cy], z: 0 }, { kind: 'tool', tool: 'riceball', n: 2, at: [cx, cy] }],\n316\t  bells: [[cx, cy]], barracks: [[cx, cy]],          // alarm bell spots; where reinforcements come out\n317\t  interact: [{ id: 'lever', at: [cx, cy], hold: 1.2, text: 'Open the water gate', do: [['open', cx, cy, w, h]] }],\n318\t  escort: { id: 'tobei', at: [cx, cy], hp: 60 },\n319\t  boss: { id: 'gonroku', at: [cx, cy], arena: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], start: 'trigger:court' },\n320\t  objectives: [{ id: 'kill', type: 'assassinate', target: 'kanemori', text: 'Silence Magistrate Kanemori' },\n321\t               { id: 'letter', type: 'retrieve', pickup: 'ledger', optional: true, text: 'Find what he hides' },\n322\t               { id: 'escape', type: 'reach', exit: true, after: ['kill', 'boss'], text: 'Escape by the canal boat' }],\n323\t  triggers: [{ id: 'court', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], once: true,\n324\t               do: [['checkpoint'], ['boss', 'gonroku'], ['say', 'gonroku', 'gon_intro']] }],\n325\t  timer: null,            // { seconds: 720, fail: 'text', stopOn: 'objective:sake' }\n326\t  par: 600, music: 'm1', weather: null }\n327\t```\n328\t\n329\tTrigger conditions:\n330\t\n331\t- `rect` / `at+r` (enter);\n332\t- `when: 'objective:<id>'`;\n333\t- `'kill:<id>'`;\n334\t- `'alert'`;\n335\t- `'time:<s>'`;\n336\t- `'pickup:<id>'`.\n337\t\n338\tTrigger actions:\n339\t\n340\t- `say`, `toast`, `tutorial`;\n341\t- `checkpoint`;\n342\t- `spawn` (a guard spec);\n343\t- `boss`, `cutscene`;\n344\t- `objective` (`show` | `done` | `fail`);\n345\t- `open` / `close` (`map.set` cells);\n346\t- `music` (layer);\n347\t- `flag`.\n348\t\n349\t**Default legend** (rows are terrain; actors are listed in the entity arrays):\n350\t\n351\t| Char | What | Rule |\n352\t|---|---|---|\n353\t| `.` | earth path | normal footsteps |\n354\t| `,` | tall grass | hide: crouched exposure ×0.15, standing ×0.6 |\n355\t| `\"` | bamboo grove | hide like grass; bamboo props scattered automatically (seeded by cell) |\n356\t| `:` | raked gravel | noise ×1.6; even crouch-walking makes noise 12 |\n357\t| `=` | wooden boards (engawa, pier) | noise ×1.2 when running; creak sfx |\n358\t| `_` | tatami (inside halls) | noise ×0.6 |\n359\t| `+` | stone paving | normal |\n360\t| `~` | deep water | swim/dive; guards and hounds never enter (nav map blocks it) |\n361\t| `-` | shallow water | wade: speed ×0.7, splash noise 40 even walking, no hiding |\n362\t| `#` | castle / outer stone wall (ishigaki) | h 56, face granite stone, top slab, `cut: true, cutH: 8`; grapple only |\n363\t| `W` | compound wall, plaster with tile cap | h 30 (climbable ledge), face plaster, roof tiles, `cut: true, cutH: 6` |\n364\t| `F` | bamboo fence | h 14 (vaulted at a run) |\n365\t| `H` | hall wall (enterable building perimeter) | h 40, face timber with shoji `decorate`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`; its roof cap is visual (section 5.18) |\n366\t| `d` | doorway in a hall wall | floor `door`; drawn as an open sliding door |\n367\t| `A` | townhouse (machiya) | h 40, plaster and timber with lattice, kawara roof (walkable) |\n368\t| `B` | two-story house or inn | h 64, timber and plaster, balcony, kawara roof |\n369\t| `C` | storehouse (kura) | h 48, white plaster with a namako band, heavy kawara roof |\n370\t| `D` | shop with noren curtain | h 40, timber, noren `decorate`, kawara roof |\n371\t| `S` | shrine or temple hall | h 56, vermilion pillars, dark kawara roof |\n372\t| `T` | watchtower (yagura), 2×2 | h 80, plank, small roof; archers stand on top |\n373\t| `G` / `K` / `M` | castle keep tiers | h 64 / 112 / 160; ishigaki base to z 24, then white plaster; chidori gables; golden shachihoko on `M` |\n374\t| `P` | planter or stone platform | h 10 (jump up; cover when crouched behind it) |\n375\t| `R` | rocks | h 20, face rock, climbable |\n376\t\n377\tEvery solid building has a flat walkable top at its height. \"No passages under things\" is an engine rule, so halls are\n378\tenterable but their roofs are not walkable.\n379\t\n380\t**Guard / enemy archetype** (`def('enemy', id, spec)`):\n381\t\n382\t```js\n383\t{ rig, hp, walk, run, sight: { range, fov, lookUp }, hear, smell, moves: [...], ranged, climbs, faction, barks,\n384\t  canSilentCut: true }\n385\t```\n386\t\n387\t**Tool** (`def('tool', id, spec)`):\n388\t\n389\t```js\n390\t{ name, icon, stack, use: 'eat' | 'throw' | 'lob' | 'drop' | 'self', range, effect(ctx), unlock }\n391\t```\n392\t\n393\t**Mission** (`def('mission', id, spec)`):\n394\t\n395\t```js\n396\t{ title, level, briefing, debrief, loadoutHint: [...], par, next, unlocks: [{ tool, rank }] }\n397\t```\n398\t\n399\t---\n400\t\n401\t## 4. Controls and UX: controller first, 10 feet from a TV\n402\t\n403\t### 4.1 Action map (`B.INPUT`, passed as `new E.Game({ input })`; every action is rebindable on the standard Controls screen)\n404\t\n405\t| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse | Notes |\n406\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n407\t| Move | Left stick (tilt <55% = quiet walk) | Left stick | WASD / arrows | in play the d-pad does **not** move: the hero reads the stick and keys only |\n408\t| Camera | Right stick: ←/→ flick turns 45°, ↑/↓ zooms | Right stick | Q / E turn 45°, − / = zoom; mouse leans the view toward the cursor | R3 / X resets the camera |\n409\t| Jump · climb · vault | ✕ (Pad0) | A | Space | parkour first (ledge ≤ 30, vault ≤ 14, gap leap) |\n410\t| Crouch (toggle; hold in Settings) | ○ (Pad1) | B | C | **never bind Ctrl**: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab |\n411\t| Strike · Silent Cut · riposte | □ (Pad2) | X | Left click / J | context: the prompt says which |\n412\t| Interact (drag body, pick up, open, talk, lever) | △ (Pad3) | Y | F (or left click on a highlighted thing) | |\n413\t| Block (hold) · parry (timed) | L1 (Pad4) | LB | Right click / K | block + jump + direction = dodge roll |\n414\t| Grappling hook (tap: fire at the highlighted anchor; hold: aim) | R1 (Pad5) | RB | G / middle click | with the mouse: the anchor under the cursor |\n415\t| Ki Focus (hold) | L2 (Pad6) | LT | Tab | slows to a walk; sense radius 220; right stick or mouse scouts further |\n416\t| Use tool | R2 (Pad7) | RT | R | thrown at the cursor (mouse) or auto-aimed (pad/keys) |\n417\t| Sprint | L3 (Pad10, a toggle until the stick is released) | LS | Shift (hold) | stamina |\n418\t| Previous / next tool | D-pad ← / → | D-pad | mouse wheel, 1–8 picks a compartment | |\n419\t| Eat a rice ball (quick heal) | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | H | |\n420\t| Whistle (lure) | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | V | noise 70 at the hero: lures nearby guards to search |\n421\t| Objectives | Create (Pad8) | View | M | shows the objectives panel (in a hub session Create does nothing: the hub owns Create + Options) |\n422\t| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Menu | Esc / P | engine standard (hub: ignored while Create is held) |\n423\t| Menus | d-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A / B | arrows, Enter, Esc; mouse hover focuses, click picks | |\n424\t\n425\tImplementation notes:\n426\t\n427\t- Action names, in `B.INPUT` and on the Controls screen (`menu.controls` gives the names):\n428\t\n429\t  | Action | Controls name |\n430\t  |---|---|\n431\t  | `jump` | Jump / climb |\n432\t  | `crouch` | Crouch |\n433\t  | `attack` | Strike / Silent Cut |\n434\t  | `interact` | Interact |\n435\t  | `block` | Block / parry |\n436\t  | `grapple` | Grappling hook |\n437\t  | `focus` | Ki Focus |\n438\t  | `useTool` | Use tool |\n439\t  | `sprint` | Sprint |\n440\t  | `toolPrev` | Previous tool |\n441\t  | `toolNext` | Next tool |\n442\t  | `heal` | Eat rice ball |\n443\t  | `lure` | Whistle |\n444\t  | `camLeft` | Turn camera left |\n445\t  | `camRight` | Turn camera right |\n446\t  | `camReset` | Reset camera |\n447\t  | `objectives` | Objectives |\n448\t\n449\t  The engine adds `up/down/left/right/start/pause/confirm/cancel`. Its menu actions `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z,\n450\t  pad A) and `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B) overlap some play keys; that is harmless, because play never\n451\t  reads them.\n452\t- Movement in play is `B.intentFromInput()`: the left stick from `input.padAxes` with the radial deadzone, plus the\n453\t  key codes of the `up/down/left/right` actions that are not `Pad*`, through `game.view.screenDirToGround`. Menus still\n454\t  use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the d-pad.\n455\t- Tool cycling with the wheel: set `camera.wheel: false` on the mission scene and add a passive `wheel` listener that\n456\t  taps `toolPrev` / `toolNext`.\n457\t- `input.lastDevice` decides prompts. A mouse used in the last 3 s means \"mouse mode\": cursor aiming, hover highlights\n458\t  and camera lean. A stick or key press ends it.\n459\t- Mouse in the world:\n460\t  - Hovering a guard shows its awareness meter and type label.\n461\t  - Hovering a highlighted interactable within reach changes the left click from Strike to Interact.\n462\t  - Hovering a valid roof edge or anchor highlights it for G / middle click.\n463\t  - Strikes face the cursor (Diablo-style).\n464\t  - Thrown tools land at `game.mouseGround()`, clamped to range.\n465\t\n466\t### 4.2 Glyphs and prompts (`03-glyphs.js`)\n467\t\n468\t- Every prompt, tutorial card, menu footer and dialog token follows the last device used, and redraws the moment it\n469\t  changes.\n470\t- **Pad (PlayStation):** a dark circle with a colored symbol: ✕ blue `#7ab4ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8`,\n471\t  △ green `#5ae0a0`.\n472\t- **Pad (Xbox):** A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow.\n473\t- **Shoulders, triggers and buttons:** L1/R1/L2/R2 (LB/RB/LT/RT) are rounded tabs. Sticks are rings with an arrow.\n474\t  The d-pad is a cross with the used arm lit. Create/Options (View/Menu) are pills.\n475\t- **Keyboard:** a light keycap with `input.codeLabel(code)`.\n476\t- **Mouse:** a mouse icon with the left, right or middle button lit, or the wheel.\n477\t- Icons are 9–11 game pixels tall and drawn with `E.px` (no font dependency). Canvas text can embed `{a:attack}`,\n478\t  which renders that action's icon inline.\n479\t- HTML (Shell) text uses `input.label()` (Unicode is fine there).\n480\t\n481\t### 4.3 Screens (big, sparse, one decision per screen; never dense web-style tables)\n482\t\n483\tCanvas screens use `E.Menu`, which already moves its cursor on hover and picks on click. HTML screens (pause, settings,\n484\tcontrols, dev, objectives, Workshop menus, About) use one `E.Shell` with this theme:\n485\t\n486\t```js\n487\t{ ink: '#f4ead5', paper: 'rgba(20,12,12,.92)', accent: '#e8b04a', muted: '#b8a890', danger: '#d8402a',\n488\t  line: 'rgba(232,176,74,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' }\n489\t```\n490\t\n491\t- **Title** (canvas, side view):\n492\t  - A night sky with a big moon over a castle silhouette (custom `E.Backdrop`: moon, stars, mountains, castle, fog).\n493\t  - Sojiro and Kaede on a tiled ridge in front, scarves fluttering, cherry petals falling.\n494\t  - The logo is `E.font.title('BENTOU 2', … { scale: 4, colors: gold → vermilion, depth: 3 })` with the subtitle below\n495\t    and the clan crest stamp.\n496\t  - \"PRESS {a:start}\" first, then the `E.Menu`: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings\n497\t    (`game.menu('settings')`) · About. Missing items are hidden (no Continue without a save).\n498\t  - Version line: `E.versionLabel()` + game version, small, bottom right.\n499\t- **Character select:**\n500\t  - Two rigs on a rooftop, side by side; ←/→ or hover picks one.\n501\t  - Name, weapon, three short bars (Strength, Speed, Stealth) and one sentence.\n502\t  - A spoken gibberish greeting with a subtitle.\n503\t- **Mission select:** a vertical list of unlocked missions on a scroll. Each shows its best rank stamp per character\n504\t  and the character toggle (L1/R1).\n505\t- **Briefing:**\n506\t  - A painted interior (the shop's back room: shoji, stacked boxes, a lantern; or the lord's moonlit garden) with live\n507\t    portraits (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n508\t  - `E.Dialog` lines with names and voices, then an objectives card (2–3 lines).\n509\t  - Hold {a:start} to skip.\n510\t- **Pack the Bento:**\n511\t  - A black-lacquer two-tier box seen from above; each tier has 4 compartments.\n512\t  - The left column is the tool shelf (big icons, name, one-line effect). The stick moves, ✕ fills the focused\n513\t    compartment, ○ empties it, △ restores the mission's suggested loadout, Options starts.\n514\t  - Mouse: hover focuses, click places, right click empties.\n515\t  - Shows each stack count. The last loadout is remembered.\n516\t- **Results:**\n517\t  - A scroll unrolls. One stat line appears at a time with a brush underline: Time, Silent Cuts, Kills, Times detected,\n518\t    Civilians harmed, Optional tasks, Tools used, Retries. Then the score counts up.\n519\t  - The rank hanko slams down (screen thump, stamp sound).\n520\t  - Granny's one-line comment, and a \"New tool\" card if one unlocked.\n521\t  - Buttons: Continue · Retry · Missions.\n522\t- **Game over overlay:** time slows, the screen desaturates, \"YOUR BOX IS EMPTY\" in brush type, and three choices.\n523\t- **About / Credits:** paged (◀ ▶), one section per page, large type (section 5.23).\n524\t- **Ending:** cutscene, then a credits roll over the moon. Any input speeds it up; it returns to the title.\n525\t\n526\t### 4.4 In-game HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` / `r.H`, inside 4% overscan margins)\n527\t\n528\t| Where | Element |\n529\t|---|---|\n530\t| top left | health bar (brush stroke in vermilion, the character's crest at its head); below it **静斬 ×n** (Silent Cut count) |\n531\t| top center | objective toast on change (fades after 4 s); the boss bar (wide, the name in brush caps, phase ticks); \"ALARM!\" banner |\n532\t| top right | M3 moon timer (an arc with the moon's position; turns red under 60 s); place name on entering a zone (fades) |\n533\t| bottom left | **Ki Gauge**: an 18-px-radius semicircle with the number 0–99 in large digits (font scale 2), a colored ring and `?`/`!`; the eye icon in its middle shows your light (closed = shadow, half = dim, open = lit) |\n534\t| bottom right | **tool box**: the selected tool's icon (16 px at scale 2) with its count; neighbors slide by on change; d-pad glyphs |\n535\t| bottom center | context prompts (at most 2): icon + label (\"□ Silent Cut — Back\", \"R1 Grapple\", \"△ Drag body\", \"△ Hold: open gate\" with a progress ring) |\n536\t| over the hero | breath bubbles when diving; a stamina ring when <100 |\n537\t| over guards | `?` yellow (notice), `?` orange (search), `!` red (alert), `Zz` (asleep), `…` (eating), with a small suspicion bar; tinted by Shadow Sight state |\n538\t| screen edges | red chevrons toward alerted enemies off screen; `r.marker` objective diamond (Settings: Objective marker) |\n539\t| cinematic | letterbox bars (Silent Cuts, boss intros, cutscenes); the 静斬 splash; a red edge pulse when hit |\n540\t\n541\tThe objectives panel (Create/M) is an `E.Shell` screen: the mission title, objectives with checkmarks, the time, and\n542\tSilent Cuts so far. In the pause menu it is \"Objectives\".\n543\t\n544\t### 4.5 Touch-only devices\n545\t\n546\t- Detection: `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, with no gamepad connected\n547\t  and no key pressed yet.\n548\t- Then: `input.touchEnabled = false`, and no scene declares touch buttons.\n549\t- The title replaces its menu with a large panel: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, a line (\"Connect a controller\n550\t  or a keyboard to play.\"), and a big **Settings** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). The engine corner menu button\n551\t  stays.\n552\t- Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual, and a tap returns to the title.\n553\t- `gamepadconnected` or any key press removes the notice at once.\n554\t\n555\t### 4.6 Settings (the engine's standard screens plus ours in group \"Game\"; Sound gets \"Voices\")\n556\t\n557\t| Setting | Values (default first) |\n558\t|---|---|\n559\t| Button symbols *(engine, patched)* | PlayStation · Xbox |\n560\t| Interface size | Auto · Normal · Large · Huge |\n561\t| Difficulty | Ninja · Novice · Grand Master: guard perception ×1 / .8 / 1.2, damage taken ×1 / .6 / 1.4, Ki range ×1 / 1.2 / .85 |\n562\t| Camera angle | Low (iso) · High (threequarter) |\n563\t| Invert camera turn | Off · On |\n564\t| Crouch | Toggle · Hold |\n565\t| Sight cones | On · Off (the faint cones of guards you can see) |\n566\t| Objective marker | On · Off |\n567\t| Show all enemies (assist) | Off · On (Shadow Sight off) |\n568\t| Ki heartbeat | On · Off |\n569\t| Text speed | Normal · Slow · Fast |\n570\t| Blood | Ink · Off (red ink splashes and decals) |\n571\t| Voices *(Sound)* | slider 0–1, default .8 |\n572\t\n573\t### 4.7 Camera\n574\t\n575\t- `game.follow(hero, { z: 18, lead: 10 })`, `cam.smooth = .12`, `cam.bounds = v => world.map.bounds(v)`.\n576\t- **Turn:** `game.rotateView(±45)` with a .25 s cooldown and a short whoosh. The compass on the tool box shows north.\n577\t  Movement stays screen-relative through `screenDirToGround`.\n578\t- **Zoom:** .75–2×, starting at 1.15 (1.35 on a tall screen). Right stick ↑/↓ or −/=.\n579\t- **Look-ahead:** mouse mode leans the focus toward the cursor by up to 40 units (140 with Focus). Pad: Focus + right\n580\t  stick pans up to 140 units, eased back on release.\n581\t- **Cinematics:**\n582\t  - Silent Cut: zoom tween to 1.8× in .15 s, `timeScale = T('slowmo')` for .55 s, letterbox, then restore.\n583\t  - Boss intro: a `game.tween` pan to the boss, the name card, then a pan back.\n584\t  - Cutscenes: scripted focus and zoom.\n585\t  - Respect Reduce motion: no shake, shorter zooms.\n586\t- **Occlusion:**\n587\t  - The hero always draws with `xray: { actors: true }`. Visible guards draw with `xray: { color: <awareness color> }`.\n588\t  - Walls nearest the camera use `cut`.\n589\t  - Hall roof caps fade while the hero is inside that hall (section 5.18).\n590\t\n591\t---\n592\t\n593\t## 5. Systems\n594\t\n595\tNumbers marked *T* are live dev sliders (section 5.20). Every system emits bus events and is covered by tests (section 9).\n596\t\n597\t### 5.1 Hero, intent and traversal (`40-hero.js`)\n598\t\n599\t**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"0f1e2a22-a8d3-45f2-8c63-d92ad71ad8d5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:15.081Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 3.6 Data formats (the campaign and the Workshop share them exactly)\n\n**Level** (`def('level', id, spec)`; the Workshop exports the same JSON):\n\n```js\n{ id: 'm1', name: 'Rice and Ash', size: [56, 48], time: 'night' /* dusk | night | rain | festival */, ambient: .38,\n  rows: ['########…', …],                 // terrain only, default legend below (48 strings of 56 chars)\n  zones: [{ id: 'mansion', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], name: 'Kanemori Mansion' }],   // HUD place names\n  lights: [{ at: [cx, cy], z: 18, r: 64, i: .9, color: '#ffb060', kind: 'stoneLantern' }],   // kind also places its prop\n  props: [['stoneLantern', cx, cy, { facing: 0 }], ['bamboo', cx, cy], …],   // solid unless { solid: false }\n  anchors: [[cx, cy, z]],                // extra grapple anchors (tree crowns, beams); roof edges are found automatically\n  hero: { at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 0 }, exit: { at: [cx, cy], r: 1.5 },\n  guards: [{ id: 'g1', type: 'ashigaru', at: [cx, cy], z: 0, facing: 90, mode: 'patrol', lantern: true,\n             route: [[cx, cy, wait, lookDeg], …], loop: true, partner: null, faction: 'kanemori' }],\n  civilians: [{ id: 'c1', type: 'maid', at: [cx, cy], mode: 'idle', route: null, disguised: false }],\n  pickups: [{ id: 'ledger', kind: 'story', at: [cx, cy], z: 0 }, { kind: 'tool', tool: 'riceball', n: 2, at: [cx, cy] }],\n  bells: [[cx, cy]], barracks: [[cx, cy]],          // alarm bell spots; where reinforcements come out\n  interact: [{ id: 'lever', at: [cx, cy], hold: 1.2, text: 'Open the water gate', do: [['open', cx, cy, w, h]] }],\n  escort: { id: 'tobei', at: [cx, cy], hp: 60 },\n  boss: { id: 'gonroku', at: [cx, cy], arena: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], start: 'trigger:court' },\n  objectives: [{ id: 'kill', type: 'assassinate', target: 'kanemori', text: 'Silence Magistrate Kanemori' },\n               { id: 'letter', type: 'retrieve', pickup: 'ledger', optional: true, text: 'Find what he hides' },\n               { id: 'escape', type: 'reach', exit: true, after: ['kill', 'boss'], text: 'Escape by the canal boat' }],\n  triggers: [{ id: 'court', rect: [cx0, cy0, cx1, cy1], once: true,\n               do: [['checkpoint'], ['boss', 'gonroku'], ['say', 'gonroku', 'gon_intro']] }],\n  timer: null,            // { seconds: 720, fail: 'text', stopOn: 'objective:sake' }\n  par: 600, music: 'm1', weather: null }\n```\n\nTrigger conditions:\n\n- `rect` / `at+r` (enter);\n- `when: 'objective:<id>'`;\n- `'kill:<id>'`;\n- `'alert'`;\n- `'time:<s>'`;\n- `'pickup:<id>'`.\n\nTrigger actions:\n\n- `say`, `toast`, `tutorial`;\n- `checkpoint`;\n- `spawn` (a guard spec);\n- `boss`, `cutscene`;\n- `objective` (`show` | `done` | `fail`);\n- `open` / `close` (`map.set` cells);\n- `music` (layer);\n- `flag`.\n\n**Default legend** (rows are terrain; actors are listed in the entity arrays):\n\n| Char | What | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `.` | earth path | normal footsteps |\n| `,` | tall grass | hide: crouched exposure ×0.15, standing ×0.6 |\n| `\"` | bamboo grove | hide like grass; bamboo props scattered automatically (seeded by cell) |\n| `:` | raked gravel | noise ×1.6; even crouch-walking makes noise 12 |\n| `=` | wooden boards (engawa, pier) | noise ×1.2 when running; creak sfx |\n| `_` | tatami (inside halls) | noise ×0.6 |\n| `+` | stone paving | normal |\n| `~` | deep water | swim/dive; guards and hounds never enter (nav map blocks it) |\n| `-` | shallow water | wade: speed ×0.7, splash noise 40 even walking, no hiding |\n| `#` | castle / outer stone wall (ishigaki) | h 56, face granite stone, top slab, `cut: true, cutH: 8`; grapple only |\n| `W` | compound wall, plaster with tile cap | h 30 (climbable ledge), face plaster, roof tiles, `cut: true, cutH: 6` |\n| `F` | bamboo fence | h 14 (vaulted at a run) |\n| `H` | hall wall (enterable building perimeter) | h 40, face timber with shoji `decorate`, `cut: true, cutH: 6`; its roof cap is visual (section 5.18) |\n| `d` | doorway in a hall wall | floor `door`; drawn as an open sliding door |\n| `A` | townhouse (machiya) | h 40, plaster and timber with lattice, kawara roof (walkable) |\n| `B` | two-story house or inn | h 64, timber and plaster, balcony, kawara roof |\n| `C` | storehouse (kura) | h 48, white plaster with a namako band, heavy kawara roof |\n| `D` | shop with noren curtain | h 40, timber, noren `decorate`, kawara roof |\n| `S` | shrine or temple hall | h 56, vermilion pillars, dark kawara roof |\n| `T` | watchtower (yagura), 2×2 | h 80, plank, small roof; archers stand on top |\n| `G` / `K` / `M` | castle keep tiers | h 64 / 112 / 160; ishigaki base to z 24, then white plaster; chidori gables; golden shachihoko on `M` |\n| `P` | planter or stone platform | h 10 (jump up; cover when crouched behind it) |\n| `R` | rocks | h 20, face rock, climbable |\n\nEvery solid building has a flat walkable top at its height. \"No passages under things\" is an engine rule, so halls are\nenterable but their roofs are not walkable.\n\n**Guard / enemy archetype** (`def('enemy', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ rig, hp, walk, run, sight: { range, fov, lookUp }, hear, smell, moves: [...], ranged, climbs, faction, barks,\n  canSilentCut: true }\n```\n\n**Tool** (`def('tool', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ name, icon, stack, use: 'eat' | 'throw' | 'lob' | 'drop' | 'self', range, effect(ctx), unlock }\n```\n\n**Mission** (`def('mission', id, spec)`):\n\n```js\n{ title, level, briefing, debrief, loadoutHint: [...], par, next, unlocks: [{ tool, rank }] }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Controls and UX: controller first, 10 feet from a TV\n\n### 4.1 Action map (`B.INPUT`, passed as `new E.Game({ input })`; every action is rebindable on the standard Controls screen)\n\n| Action | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (Settings) | Keyboard + mouse | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Move | Left stick (tilt <55% = quiet walk) | Left stick | WASD / arrows | in play the d-pad does **not** move: the hero reads the stick and keys only |\n| Camera | Right stick: ←/→ flick turns 45°, ↑/↓ zooms | Right stick | Q / E turn 45°, − / = zoom; mouse leans the view toward the cursor | R3 / X resets the camera |\n| Jump · climb · vault | ✕ (Pad0) | A | Space | parkour first (ledge ≤ 30, vault ≤ 14, gap leap) |\n| Crouch (toggle; hold in Settings) | ○ (Pad1) | B | C | **never bind Ctrl**: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab |\n| Strike · Silent Cut · riposte | □ (Pad2) | X | Left click / J | context: the prompt says which |\n| Interact (drag body, pick up, open, talk, lever) | △ (Pad3) | Y | F (or left click on a highlighted thing) | |\n| Block (hold) · parry (timed) | L1 (Pad4) | LB | Right click / K | block + jump + direction = dodge roll |\n| Grappling hook (tap: fire at the highlighted anchor; hold: aim) | R1 (Pad5) | RB | G / middle click | with the mouse: the anchor under the cursor |\n| Ki Focus (hold) | L2 (Pad6) | LT | Tab | slows to a walk; sense radius 220; right stick or mouse scouts further |\n| Use tool | R2 (Pad7) | RT | R | thrown at the cursor (mouse) or auto-aimed (pad/keys) |\n| Sprint | L3 (Pad10, a toggle until the stick is released) | LS | Shift (hold) | stamina |\n| Previous / next tool | D-pad ← / → | D-pad | mouse wheel, 1–8 picks a compartment | |\n| Eat a rice ball (quick heal) | D-pad ↓ | D-pad ↓ | H | |\n| Whistle (lure) | D-pad ↑ | D-pad ↑ | V | noise 70 at the hero: lures nearby guards to search |\n| Objectives | Create (Pad8) | View | M | shows the objectives panel (in a hub session Create does nothing: the hub owns Create + Options) |\n| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Menu | Esc / P | engine standard (hub: ignored while Create is held) |\n| Menus | d-pad / stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | A / B | arrows, Enter, Esc; mouse hover focuses, click picks | |\n\nImplementation notes:\n\n- Action names, in `B.INPUT` and on the Controls screen (`menu.controls` gives the names):\n\n  | Action | Controls name |\n  |---|---|\n  | `jump` | Jump / climb |\n  | `crouch` | Crouch |\n  | `attack` | Strike / Silent Cut |\n  | `interact` | Interact |\n  | `block` | Block / parry |\n  | `grapple` | Grappling hook |\n  | `focus` | Ki Focus |\n  | `useTool` | Use tool |\n  | `sprint` | Sprint |\n  | `toolPrev` | Previous tool |\n  | `toolNext` | Next tool |\n  | `heal` | Eat rice ball |\n  | `lure` | Whistle |\n  | `camLeft` | Turn camera left |\n  | `camRight` | Turn camera right |\n  | `camReset` | Reset camera |\n  | `objectives` | Objectives |\n\n  The engine adds `up/down/left/right/start/pause/confirm/cancel`. Its menu actions `confirm` (Enter, Space, J, Z,\n  pad A) and `cancel` (Escape, Backspace, X, K, pad B) overlap some play keys; that is harmless, because play never\n  reads them.\n- Movement in play is `B.intentFromInput()`: the left stick from `input.padAxes` with the radial deadzone, plus the\n  key codes of the `up/down/left/right` actions that are not `Pad*`, through `game.view.screenDirToGround`. Menus still\n  use the engine's `up/down/left/right`, which include the d-pad.\n- Tool cycling with the wheel: set `camera.wheel: false` on the mission scene and add a passive `wheel` listener that\n  taps `toolPrev` / `toolNext`.\n- `input.lastDevice` decides prompts. A mouse used in the last 3 s means \"mouse mode\": cursor aiming, hover highlights\n  and camera lean. A stick or key press ends it.\n- Mouse in the world:\n  - Hovering a guard shows its awareness meter and type label.\n  - Hovering a highlighted interactable within reach changes the left click from Strike to Interact.\n  - Hovering a valid roof edge or anchor highlights it for G / middle click.\n  - Strikes face the cursor (Diablo-style).\n  - Thrown tools land at `game.mouseGround()`, clamped to range.\n\n### 4.2 Glyphs and prompts (`03-glyphs.js`)\n\n- Every prompt, tutorial card, menu footer and dialog token follows the last device used, and redraws the moment it\n  changes.\n- **Pad (PlayStation):** a dark circle with a colored symbol: ✕ blue `#7ab4ff`, ○ red `#ff6a6a`, □ pink `#ff8ad8`,\n  △ green `#5ae0a0`.\n- **Pad (Xbox):** A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow.\n- **Shoulders, triggers and buttons:** L1/R1/L2/R2 (LB/RB/LT/RT) are rounded tabs. Sticks are rings with an arrow.\n  The d-pad is a cross with the used arm lit. Create/Options (View/Menu) are pills.\n- **Keyboard:** a light keycap with `input.codeLabel(code)`.\n- **Mouse:** a mouse icon with the left, right or middle button lit, or the wheel.\n- Icons are 9–11 game pixels tall and drawn with `E.px` (no font dependency). Canvas text can embed `{a:attack}`,\n  which renders that action's icon inline.\n- HTML (Shell) text uses `input.label()` (Unicode is fine there).\n\n### 4.3 Screens (big, sparse, one decision per screen; never dense web-style tables)\n\nCanvas screens use `E.Menu`, which already moves its cursor on hover and picks on click. HTML screens (pause, settings,\ncontrols, dev, objectives, Workshop menus, About) use one `E.Shell` with this theme:\n\n```js\n{ ink: '#f4ead5', paper: 'rgba(20,12,12,.92)', accent: '#e8b04a', muted: '#b8a890', danger: '#d8402a',\n  line: 'rgba(232,176,74,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif', titleFont: 'Georgia, \"Times New Roman\", serif' }\n```\n\n- **Title** (canvas, side view):\n  - A night sky with a big moon over a castle silhouette (custom `E.Backdrop`: moon, stars, mountains, castle, fog).\n  - Sojiro and Kaede on a tiled ridge in front, scarves fluttering, cherry petals falling.\n  - The logo is `E.font.title('BENTOU 2', … { scale: 4, colors: gold → vermilion, depth: 3 })` with the subtitle below\n    and the clan crest stamp.\n  - \"PRESS {a:start}\" first, then the `E.Menu`: Continue · New Story · Missions · Shadow Trial · Workshop · Settings\n    (`game.menu('settings')`) · About. Missing items are hidden (no Continue without a save).\n  - Version line: `E.versionLabel()` + game version, small, bottom right.\n- **Character select:**\n  - Two rigs on a rooftop, side by side; ←/→ or hover picks one.\n  - Name, weapon, three short bars (Strength, Speed, Stealth) and one sentence.\n  - A spoken gibberish greeting with a subtitle.\n- **Mission select:** a vertical list of unlocked missions on a scroll. Each shows its best rank stamp per character\n  and the character toggle (L1/R1).\n- **Briefing:**\n  - A painted interior (the shop's back room: shoji, stacked boxes, a lantern; or the lord's moonlit garden) with live\n    portraits (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n  - `E.Dialog` lines with names and voices, then an objectives card (2–3 lines).\n  - Hold {a:start} to skip.\n- **Pack the Bento:**\n  - A black-lacquer two-tier box seen from above; each tier has 4 compartments.\n  - The left column is the tool shelf (big icons, name, one-line effect). The stick moves, ✕ fills the focused\n    compartment, ○ empties it, △ restores the mission's suggested loadout, Options starts.\n  - Mouse: hover focuses, click places, right click empties.\n  - Shows each stack count. The last loadout is remembered.\n- **Results:**\n  - A scroll unrolls. One stat line appears at a time with a brush underline: Time, Silent Cuts, Kills, Times detected,\n    Civilians harmed, Optional tasks, Tools used, Retries. Then the score counts up.\n  - The rank hanko slams down (screen thump, stamp sound).\n  - Granny's one-line comment, and a \"New tool\" card if one unlocked.\n  - Buttons: Continue · Retry · Missions.\n- **Game over overlay:** time slows, the screen desaturates, \"YOUR BOX IS EMPTY\" in brush type, and three choices.\n- **About / Credits:** paged (◀ ▶), one section per page, large type (section 5.23).\n- **Ending:** cutscene, then a credits roll over the moon. Any input speeds it up; it returns to the title.\n\n### 4.4 In-game HUD (canvas, anchored to `r.W` / `r.H`, inside 4% overscan margins)\n\n| Where | Element |\n|---|---|\n| top left | health bar (brush stroke in vermilion, the character's crest at its head); below it **静斬 ×n** (Silent Cut count) |\n| top center | objective toast on change (fades after 4 s); the boss bar (wide, the name in brush caps, phase ticks); \"ALARM!\" banner |\n| top right | M3 moon timer (an arc with the moon's position; turns red under 60 s); place name on entering a zone (fades) |\n| bottom left | **Ki Gauge**: an 18-px-radius semicircle with the number 0–99 in large digits (font scale 2), a colored ring and `?`/`!`; the eye icon in its middle shows your light (closed = shadow, half = dim, open = lit) |\n| bottom right | **tool box**: the selected tool's icon (16 px at scale 2) with its count; neighbors slide by on change; d-pad glyphs |\n| bottom center | context prompts (at most 2): icon + label (\"□ Silent Cut — Back\", \"R1 Grapple\", \"△ Drag body\", \"△ Hold: open gate\" with a progress ring) |\n| over the hero | breath bubbles when diving; a stamina ring when <100 |\n| over guards | `?` yellow (notice), `?` orange (search), `!` red (alert), `Zz` (asleep), `…` (eating), with a small suspicion bar; tinted by Shadow Sight state |\n| screen edges | red chevrons toward alerted enemies off screen; `r.marker` objective diamond (Settings: Objective marker) |\n| cinematic | letterbox bars (Silent Cuts, boss intros, cutscenes); the 静斬 splash; a red edge pulse when hit |\n\nThe objectives panel (Create/M) is an `E.Shell` screen: the mission title, objectives with checkmarks, the time, and\nSilent Cuts so far. In the pause menu it is \"Objectives\".\n\n### 4.5 Touch-only devices\n\n- Detection: `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, with no gamepad connected\n  and no key pressed yet.\n- Then: `input.touchEnabled = false`, and no scene declares touch buttons.\n- The title replaces its menu with a large panel: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, a line (\"Connect a controller\n  or a keyboard to play.\"), and a big **Settings** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). The engine corner menu button\n  stays.\n- Attract mode runs after 10 s as usual, and a tap returns to the title.\n- `gamepadconnected` or any key press removes the notice at once.\n\n### 4.6 Settings (the engine's standard screens plus ours in group \"Game\"; Sound gets \"Voices\")\n\n| Setting | Values (default first) |\n|---|---|\n| Button symbols *(engine, patched)* | PlayStation · Xbox |\n| Interface size | Auto · Normal · Large · Huge |\n| Difficulty | Ninja · Novice · Grand Master: guard perception ×1 / .8 / 1.2, damage taken ×1 / .6 / 1.4, Ki range ×1 / 1.2 / .85 |\n| Camera angle | Low (iso) · High (threequarter) |\n| Invert camera turn | Off · On |\n| Crouch | Toggle · Hold |\n| Sight cones | On · Off (the faint cones of guards you can see) |\n| Objective marker | On · Off |\n| Show all enemies (assist) | Off · On (Shadow Sight off) |\n| Ki heartbeat | On · Off |\n| Text speed | Normal · Slow · Fast |\n| Blood | Ink · Off (red ink splashes and decals) |\n| Voices *(Sound)* | slider 0–1, default .8 |\n\n### 4.7 Camera\n\n- `game.follow(hero, { z: 18, lead: 10 })`, `cam.smooth = .12`, `cam.bounds = v => world.map.bounds(v)`.\n- **Turn:** `game.rotateView(±45)` with a .25 s cooldown and a short whoosh. The compass on the tool box shows north.\n  Movement stays screen-relative through `screenDirToGround`.\n- **Zoom:** .75–2×, starting at 1.15 (1.35 on a tall screen). Right stick ↑/↓ or −/=.\n- **Look-ahead:** mouse mode leans the focus toward the cursor by up to 40 units (140 with Focus). Pad: Focus + right\n  stick pans up to 140 units, eased back on release.\n- **Cinematics:**\n  - Silent Cut: zoom tween to 1.8× in .15 s, `timeScale = T('slowmo')` for .55 s, letterbox, then restore.\n  - Boss intro: a `game.tween` pan to the boss, the name card, then a pan back.\n  - Cutscenes: scripted focus and zoom.\n  - Respect Reduce motion: no shake, shorter zooms.\n- **Occlusion:**\n  - The hero always draws with `xray: { actors: true }`. Visible guards draw with `xray: { color: <awareness color> }`.\n  - Walls nearest the camera use `cut`.\n  - Hall roof caps fade while the hero is inside that hall (section 5.18).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Systems\n\nNumbers marked *T* are live dev sliders (section 5.20). Every system emits bus events and is covered by tests (section 9).\n\n### 5.1 Hero, intent and traversal (`40-hero.js`)\n\n**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):","numLines":300,"startLine":300,"totalLines":1883}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QtVj8QB34RsCQq2mGJ5d15","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
