{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2GSNmKqZgQkiWGznd1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YF5xujt8zJ9H2kNLMT8Fke","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":599,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8973,"cache_read_input_tokens":471036,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8973},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"ac3f84a8-4424-4651-89d4-5ee7822676a3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:20.387Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2GS69MKdpRzVfCHxPq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YF5xujt8zJ9H2kNLMT8Fke":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":599,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YF5xujt8zJ9H2kNLMT8Fke","type":"tool_result","content":"599\t**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):\n600\t\n601\t```js\n602\t{ move: [x, y]  /* world ground dir, length 0..1 */, walk, sprint, crouchPressed, jumpPressed, attackPressed,\n603\t  blockDown, interactPressed, interactDown, grapplePressed, grappleDown, grappleReleased, usePressed, focusDown,\n604\t  toolDelta, toolSlot, healPressed, lurePressed, aimPoint /* {x,y} or null */ }\n605\t```\n606\t\n607\t**Body:**\n608\t\n609\t```js\n610\tnew E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, climbAny: false, climbMax: 30, vault: 14, hopMax: 48, staminaMax: 100,\n611\t              run: T('heroRun'), sneak: T('heroSneak'), sprintSpeed: T('heroSprint'), jumpSpeed: 220 })\n612\t```\n613\t\n614\t`climbAny` is off on purpose: roofs need the grapple, as in the source. Fed with\n615\t`{ move, sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }` each step. `rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({...}))`.\n616\t\n617\t| Mode | Speed | Noise radius (*T* `noiseRun`) | Notes |\n618\t|---|---|---|---|\n619\t| walk (stick <55% or Focus) | 50 | 0 | |\n620\t| run | *T* 85 (Kaede 92) | 60 (Kaede ×.8) | surface multipliers from the legend |\n621\t| sprint (stamina 20/s) | *T* 125 (Kaede 132) | 110 | |\n622\t| crouch (toggle) | *T* 32 | 0 (gravel 12) | `hero.chest = 8`; E.sees ×.6 built in |\n623\t| jump / land | — | land 50 (roll at 26+ drop silences it to 20) | fall >72 hurts 15 |\n624\t| swim (deep water) | 30 | 15 (splash) | no attacks or tools except eat; visible |\n625\t| dive (crouch in deep water) | 24 | 0 | **unseen** (exposure 0); breath *T* 12 s, then 8 dmg/s; bubbles |\n626\t| wall hug | 24 sideways | 0 | exposure ×.6; peek at corners |\n627\t| drag body | 24 | 10 | can't jump, strike or use tools |\n628\t\n629\t- **Wall hug:** crouched and pushing into a wall face (`map.wall(hero, dir)`) for .2 s presses the back to the wall\n630\t  (custom pose: arms flat, head turned along the wall).\n631\t  - The stick moves along the face only.\n632\t  - At a face end, the hero leans out: the camera pans 48 units past the corner, and Shadow Sight checks from a peek\n633\t    eye 10 units past the corner.\n634\t  - Push away or press ○ to leave.\n635\t- **Roll:** block + jump + direction → `hero.dodge(dir, 34)` (invulnerable mid-roll).\n636\t- **Drag:**\n637\t  - △ near a dead or asleep body grabs it under the arms. The victim's rig stays `down: 1` and is dragged 14 units\n638\t    behind, facing up. △ drops it.\n639\t  - Dropped in deep water, it sinks (splash, removed).\n640\t  - Dropped in grass, bamboo or a lightAt <.3 spot, it is hidden (body discovery needs exposure >.35).\n641\t- **Falls and hazards:** Mover's `rollAt` / `hurtAt`. Out-of-map or unwalkable spots → `hero.respawn()` (−10 HP).\n642\t- **Stats** (`def('character', …)`):\n643\t\n644\t  | | HP | Damage | Block | Silent Cut | Grapple pull | Noise |\n645\t  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n646\t  | Sojiro | 100 | ×1.2 | 85% | .9 s | ×1.0 | ×1.0 |\n647\t  | Kaede | 80 | ×.85, attacks ×1.25 faster | 70% | .7 s | ×1.15 | ×.8 |\n648\t\n649\t  The hub and Shadow Trial use equal \"trial\" stats (Sojiro's) for both looks.\n650\t\n651\t### 5.2 Grappling hook — kaginawa (`42-grapple.js`)\n652\t\n653\t- **Anchors:**\n654\t  - The auto-found ones are wall tops of solid cells whose top is between `z+16` and `z+T('grappleMaxRise')` (96),\n655\t    within `T('grappleRange')` (112) horizontally of the hero.\n656\t  - The rope line from the hand (z+28) to the edge point must be clear (`map.ray`), and the landing must be standable\n657\t    (`map.standable(edge-in by 6, top)`).\n658\t  - Plus the level's `anchors` (tree crowns, beams).\n659\t  - Hall walls `H` and keep tiers above the next tier are excluded, so every grapple lands somewhere sensible.\n660\t- **Targeting:**\n661\t  - Every .1 s, score the candidates: angle to the facing (or to the cursor / aim point) + distance.\n662\t  - The best one within a 70-degree cone gets a subtle gold diamond, plus the prompt \"R1 Grapple\".\n663\t  - Hold R1 to aim: time slows to .5, every anchor in range shows, and the stick or cursor picks one.\n664\t  - Release fires. Tap fires at the highlighted anchor.\n665\t  - In mouse mode, the anchor nearest the `map.pick` point under the cursor wins.\n666\t- **Action** `E.ACTIONS.grapple`, with beats `[['throw', .16], ['pull', dist / T('grappleSpeed')], ['mantle', .2]]`:\n667\t  - throw: the `throw` move. The rope is drawn from `rig.hand('R')` out to the hook along a sagging curve.\n668\t  - pull: the body moves along a quadratic Bezier from the start to the edge point with a 10-unit arc. The rig is\n669\t    `air: true` with hands up.\n670\t  - mantle: a hang-to-crouch pull-up onto the top, ending crouched.\n671\t  - Noise 30 at the hook. It can be fired mid-jump. Cooldown .3 s.\n672\t- **Rope drawing:** `r.queue` a 1-px line through 8 points (rope color `#c8b080`, shadowed), with a hook glint at the\n673\t  anchor.\n674\t\n675\t### 5.3 Light, shadow and cover (`30-world.js` + `50-perception.js`)\n676\t\n677\t- **Light map:** a grid of half-cells (8 units), baked in a boot step per level:\n678\t\n679\t  ```text\n680\t  L = ambientMoon + Σ i · (1 − d/r)² · LOS(light → point)     (LOS = map.los; clamp 0..1)\n681\t  ```\n682\t\n683\t  ambientMoon is `.22` at night, `.45` at dusk, `.18` in rain and `.3` at the festival.\n684\t- **Dynamic lights**, added at query time: guards' hand lanterns (r 48, i .8), fire, burning fire pots, and lightning\n685\t  flashes (rain: all exposure ×2 for .25 s; the thunder sfx follows).\n686\t- **Exposure** given to `E.sees` as `hero.exposure`:\n687\t\n688\t  ```text\n689\t  lightF = lerp(1 − T('darkness'), 1, L)\n690\t  coverF = 1 | grass/bamboo (.15 crouched / .6 standing) | dive 0 | wall hug .6 | Kakuremino .15\n691\t  motionF = still .75 | walk 1 | run 1.15 | sprint 1.3\n692\t  exposure = lightF · coverF · motionF · (crouch ? T('crouchVis') / .6 : 1)\n693\t  ```\n694\t\n695\t  The last factor turns the engine's built-in .6 for crouching into the slider value.\n696\t- **Visuals match gameplay:** every light in `lights` is also a `game.lights.add` (with flicker) and a prop.\n697\t  - Ambient: `game.lights.ambient` = .38 (night), plus a cool tint.\n698\t  - GPU lighting when available: `game.enableGPU({ map })`, which also gives wall shadows. Set both ambients so the\n699\t    canvas fallback matches.\n700\t- Dev overlay \"Light map\" draws L as a dithered heat map on the ground.\n701\t\n702\t### 5.4 Perception and guard minds (`50-perception.js`, `51-guard-brain.js`)\n703\t\n704\t- **Sight**, every step per awake guard:\n705\t\n706\t  ```js\n707\t  E.sees(g, hero, { map, range: T('sightRange') * g.sightMul, fov: T('sightFov'), eye })\n708\t  ```\n709\t\n710\t  then exposure as above, and two gates:\n711\t  - **Look-up limit:** if the hero is >16 above the guard's eyes and the elevation angle is above `T('lookUp')`\n712\t    (35 degrees), the guard can't see. Archers and ninja ignore this.\n713\t  - **Smoke:** if the sight segment passes within a cloud's radius, not seen.\n714\t- **Mind:**\n715\t\n716\t  ```js\n717\t  g.mind = new E.Suspicion({ rise: T('suspRise'), decay: T('suspDecay'), forget: 7 })\n718\t  ```\n719\t\n720\t  Its states are calm, notice (turn toward `mind.last`, bark), search (walk to last, look around 4 s, then a widening\n721\t  search around it) and alert (chase or fight).\n722\t  - Added game states: `post`, `sleep`, `eat` (bait), `chat` (pairs face each other and bark), `stunned`, `blinded`\n723\t    (smoke), `poisoned`, `flee` (civilians, and archers with no arrow line), `returning`.\n724\t- **Hearing:**\n725\t\n726\t  ```js\n727\t  B.noise(x, y, z, loud, kind)\n728\t  for each guard: s = E.hears(g, noise, map) * T('hearing')\n729\t  if (s > .15) g.mind.hear(s, noise)\n730\t  ```\n731\t\n732\t  Sleeping guards wake at s > .5. Hounds hear ×1.5.\n733\t- **Smell** (hounds): within 60 (crouched 40) of the hero → bark (noise 150) and notice. Diving cancels it.\n734\t  Fragrant baits within 120 attract them.\n735\t- **Bodies:**\n736\t  - A guard whose cone sees a body (`E.sees` on the body with exposure from light and cover; bodies in grass, dark or\n737\t    water don't count) within `T('bodyRange')` (96) runs to it.\n738\t  - It shouts (\"Assassin!\") → alert-shout noise. The level becomes **Heightened** for 90 s: sight range ×1.2, rise\n739\t    ×1.3, and the guard runs for the bell.\n740\t- **Barks:** each state change (and calm idles every 12–25 s) picks a line from `Story.barks[category]`. It is spoken by\n741\t  the voice synth with a world-positioned subtitle bubble (canvas, 1.5–2.5 s), at most one bark per 2 s within the\n742\t  screen.\n743\t- **Guard update order:** perceive → mind → behavior → move (`g.flow` = shared FlowField cache by goal cell, LRU 24,\n744\t  built on the **nav map**, which blocks water; ninja fields use `{ climb: 56, drop: 56, jump: 60 }`) → rig.\n745\t\n746\t### 5.5 Shadow Sight, the Ki Gauge and Ki Focus (`50-perception.js`, `70-hud.js`)\n747\t\n748\t- **Shadow Sight** (20 Hz): a guard is *visible* if `map.sight(heroEye, guard)` is true within 200 units (360 degrees;\n749\t  from the peek eye while hugging).\n750\t  - Otherwise, if within `T('kiRange')` (160), it is *sensed*: drawn as a translucent indigo silhouette\n751\t    (`alpha .35, flash '#5a5aff', flashMix 1`, no shadow, no cone), but its awareness mark still shows.\n752\t  - Otherwise it is *hidden* and not drawn.\n753\t  - Civilians follow the same rule. The setting \"Show all enemies\" and the dev \"Reveal all\" disable it.\n754\t- **Ki number:** `K = max over sensed or visible guards of round(99 · (1 − d / kiRange))`.\n755\t  - The color is the highest awareness among them: calm teal `#5ad8c8`, notice yellow `#f0d050`, search orange\n756\t    `#f09040`, alert red `#ff4a3a`.\n757\t  - The glyph is `?` or `!`.\n758\t  - At K ≥ 50, a soft taiko heartbeat (rate 0.8–2.2 Hz by K). Setting: Ki heartbeat.\n759\t- **Ki Focus** (hold L2/Tab):\n760\t  - The hero walks at most; the zoom eases to .9×; the sense radius is 220; sensed guards brighten and show their sight\n761\t    cones through walls.\n762\t  - Disguised Red Lanterns get a red aura (only way to spot them). Anchors and pickups in range glint. The world\n763\t    desaturates 30%.\n764\t  - No cost but speed.\n765\t\n766\t### 5.6 Alarm, reinforcements, Heightened\n767\t\n768\t- An alert guard shouts: noise `T('alertShout')` (160), so guards who hear it search toward the hero's position.\n769\t- If a bell is within 240 nav units, the shouting guard (or the first to find a body) **runs to the bell**. After 1.5 s\n770\t  of ringing (a big bronze sfx, screen toast \"The alarm bell rings!\"):\n771\t  - all guards go to search at the hero's last known position;\n772\t  - the level is Heightened for the rest of the mission;\n773\t  - after `T('reinforceDelay')` (15 s), 2 reinforcements (one samurai, one ashigaru, of the level's faction) come out\n774\t    of the nearest barracks door.\n775\t  - At most 2 waves per mission.\n776\t  - Killing the runner before the ring stops it (bonus line: \"The bell stays silent.\").\n777\t- **Music:** tension layer at any notice or K ≥ 60; alert layers (taiko + fue) on any alert, faded out 4 s after the\n778\t  last alert ends (`audio.layer`).\n779\t- **Calm-down:** an alert guard that loses the hero for `forget` seconds searches, then returns to its route with a\n780\t  \"lost\" bark (\"…Must have been the wind.\"). A Heightened level never fully relaxes.\n781\t\n782\t### 5.7 Silent Cuts — 静斬 (`41-silentcut.js`)\n783\t\n784\tChecked every step for the best candidate. The prompt is \"□ Silent Cut — <kind>\", and the button runs it. Only\n785\tnon-boss enemies, and never while they are alert or in combat. `rel` is the angle between the guard's facing and the\n786\tdirection hero→guard (0 = the hero is directly behind):\n787\t\n788\t| Kind | Condition | Victim | Noise |\n789\t|---|---|---|---|\n790\t| **Back** | d ≤ *T* `killRange` 18, same level (10), rel < *T* `killBackAngle` 60° | calm, notice or search, not seeing the hero this step | 0 |\n791\t| **Side** | d ≤ 18, same level, 60° ≤ rel < 120° | calm only, not seeing the hero | 15 (grunt) |\n792\t| **Front** | d ≤ 18, same level, rel ≥ 120° | incapacitated: asleep, eating, stunned, blinded, poisoned | 15 |\n793\t| **From above** | hero on a top ≥14 above, horizontal d ≤ 44, `map.arcClear`, hero on ground | calm, notice or search | 0 |\n794\t| **Undertow** (from water) | hero swimming or diving, d ≤ 20, victim on a cell next to deep water | not alert | 10 (splash) |\n795\t\n796\t- Each kind is an `E.ACTIONS` paired action per character (copy the engine's `takedown` structure: `beats`, `setup`,\n797\t  `at` returning `{ x, y, z, state, other }`), built from `E.move(...)` poses and joint post-processing.\n798\t\n799\t  | Kind | Sojiro | Kaede |\n800\t  |---|---|---|\n801\t  | Back | `[['grab',.16],['strike',.24],['hold',.25],['drop',.4],['recover',.18]]`: left hand over the mouth (post-processed arm), `thrust` through | a hop, then two `thrust` beats (main and offhand), `drop` |\n802\t  | Side | a dash past with `slash` | a `spin` |\n803\t  | Front | a `rising` cut, the victim falls backward | an `X` cut, both blades |\n804\t  | Above | the engine's aerial leap with `overhead` | a `plunge` |\n805\t  | Undertow | rises with a `claw`-like grab and drags the victim into the water (victim slides, sinks, splash, fades) | same |\n806\t\n807\t  Victims get `hurt`, `expr: 'wince'`, then `down`.\n808\t- **Presentation:**\n809\t  - Freeze .05.\n810\t  - Camera zoom 1.8× and slow motion `T('slowmo')` for .55 s; letterbox.\n811\t  - The **静斬** splash: two 32×32 brush-kanji string sprites, red `#d02a20` with a dark edge, drawn scaled ×2 at the\n812\t    screen's center-left, with an ink-splatter burst. A small \"SILENT CUT\" caption under it.\n813\t  - A shamisen twang + reverse-swell sting; ink-splatter decals (Blood setting).\n814\t  - Restore after .9 s.\n815\t- **Effects:** `bus.emit('silentCut', { kind, victim })` gives score +150; the HUD counter goes up; hub progress\n816\t  updates.\n817\t\n818\t### 5.8 Combat (`43-combat.js`)\n819\t\n820\t- **Damage pipeline:** `B.damage(src, dst, amount, { kind, angle })` applies:\n821\t  1. multipliers: the character's damage multiplier for hero hits; difficulty × *T* `enemyDmg` for hits on the hero;\n822\t     *T* `enemyHp` scales enemy HP at spawn;\n823\t  2. block (front 120 degrees, reduces by the character's block %);\n824\t  3. i-frames (.4 s after a hit);\n825\t  4. death → `kill` or `heroDeath` events.\n826\t\n827\t  Hit feedback has **no damage numbers** (the source shows none). Check `game.hitFx`'s options for turning its number\n828\t  off; if it can't, call `game.freeze(.05)`, `game.shake`, `particles.impact`, `particles.sparks` and the hit sfx\n829\t  yourself, plus ink drops.\n830\t- **Hero melee:**\n831\t  - Sojiro: `new E.Combo(['slash','backslash','overhead'], { window: .3 })`, damage 14 / 14 / 24.\n832\t  - Kaede: `['thrust','backslash','spin']`, damage 9 / 9 / 18, at speed ×1.25.\n833\t  - Jump attack: `plunge`, 20 / 16.\n834\t  - `attack.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 20, 1.3, 10), …)`. Face the cursor in mouse mode, or the\n835\t    nearest enemy within 40 (auto-aim).\n836\t- **Block (L1 hold):** pose `block`. The guard's chip goes through at 15%.\n837\t- **Parry:** press block within `T('parryWindow')` (.18 s) before an enemy swing's active beat (the last part of its\n838\t  wind-up).\n839\t  - The enemy is staggered 1.3 s (\"staggered\" stars).\n840\t  - The prompt \"□ Riposte\" kills ashigaru, samurai and ninja instantly (a short cinematic, counted as a kill, not a\n841\t    Silent Cut) and does 60 damage to bosses.\n842\t  - A white flash, ring sfx and sparks.\n843\t- **Enemy swings:** `E.Attack(move, { wind: base × T('enemyWindup'), … })` with visible wind-ups, longer than the\n844\t  hero's. Red `groundArc` decals warn for area attacks.\n845\t- **Hero HP 0:** the `die` pose, then the game over overlay. Retry restores the last checkpoint (section 5.14).\n846\t\n847\t### 5.9 Tools and the Bento (`44-tools.js`)\n848\t\n849\tThe bento has 8 compartments (2 tiers × 4). Each holds one tool type, up to that tool's stack; the same tool may fill\n850\tseveral compartments. Stock is unlimited: what limits you is packing. The default loadout comes from the mission's\n851\t`loadoutHint`, and the last one is remembered.\n852\t\n853\t| Tool | Stack | Use | Effect (numbers are TUNE entries) | Unlock |\n854\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n855\t| **Rice Ball** (onigiri) | 3 | eat (.6 s, vulnerable) | +40 HP | start |\n856\t| **Poison Rice Ball** | 2 | drop at the feet or a short toss ≤48 | a guard or hound that sees it within *T* `baitRange` 80 (hounds smell 120) and is calm walks to it (`eat` state, back to the room), eats 2 s, then dies 3 s later (\"Ugh… my stomach…\"). Counts as a kill: +100 \"clean\" | start |\n857\t| **Sleep Dango** | 2 | same as poison | the eater sleeps 25 s (snores, noise 20). Front Silent Cut allowed | rank ≥ Ekiben in \"Rice and Ash\" |\n858\t| **Sour Plum** (umeboshi) | 3 | eat (instant) | stamina full + **soft steps** 20 s (run noise 0, sprint 30) | rank ≥ Ekiben in the Trial |\n859\t| **Shuriken** | 10 | throw (`E.Bullets` ground plane, 300 u/s, range 160) | 8 damage; a calm guard hit turns to search toward the thrower's line | start |\n860\t| **Smoke Bomb** | 2 | lob ≤96 (or at the feet with block held) | a cloud r 40 for *T* `smokeTime` 6 s blocks sight through it. Guards inside are `blinded` (cough, 1.5 s) and lose the hero (`mind.level` capped at search; last position stale). Big `particles.smoke` | start |\n861\t| **Caltrops** | 2 | drop | area r 24 for 20 s: an enemy stepping in takes 6 damage, a 2 s stun, then limps (×.5 speed, 6 s). The hero is immune | start |\n862\t| **Firecracker** | 3 | lob ≤128 | pops .8 s after landing: noise 140 at the landing, so non-alert guards search there; hounds bark | start |\n863\t| **Fire Pot** (horokudama) | 1 | lob ≤112, explodes on impact | r 32, 45 damage (the hero too if inside), noise 220 (wakes and alerts), fire particles + light 1 s | rank ≥ Makunouchi in \"Kiri Lake\" |\n864\t| **Straw Cloak** (kakuremino) | 1 | self | 15 s: sight rise ×.15 unless within 16, striking or sprinting; drawn as a straw-cloaked silhouette | Grand Kaiseki in any mission |\n865\t\n866\t- **Aiming:** thrown and lobbed tools target `intent.aimPoint` (the mouse ground point). Otherwise auto-aim at the\n867\t  nearest visible guard in a 45-degree cone within range, else 80 units ahead. Lobs use `E.arc(from, to, 700, { apex:\n868\t  24 })` on a small `E.Body` with a trail.\n869\t- Each use emits `toolUsed` (results line \"Tools used\"). Pickups in levels add to the current stacks, up to the stack.\n870\t\n871\t### 5.10 Bodies\n872\t\n873\t- Dead and asleep guards stay where they fell (rig `down: 1`). Discovery is covered in section 5.4; dragging and\n874\t  hiding in section 5.1.\n875\t- Bodies in deep water sink. A poisoned guard's body counts as found like any other.\n876\t- The dev overlay marks bodies and whether each is hidden.\n877\t\n878\t### 5.11 Enemies and civilians (`52-enemies.js`; rigs in section 6.1)\n879\t\n880\t| Type | HP | Speeds walk/run | Sight range / fov | Moves | Special |\n881\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n882\t| **Ashigaru** (spear) | 40 | 30 / 70 | ×1.0 / 1.5 | `thrust` 12 (wind .42), `overhead` butt 10 | often carries a hand lantern (lights itself: easy to see, sees well) |\n883\t| **Samurai** (katana, sashimono) | 70 | 32 / 75 | ×1.05 / 1.5 | `slash` 16 (wind .36), `overhead` 22 (wind .5), blocks frontal hits 50% | parry target; the bell-runner of choice |\n884\t| **Archer** (bow, on towers and roofs) | 30 | 28 / 65 | ×1.25 / 1.3; looks up | arrows 14 dmg, 260 u/s at chest height, 1.6 s draw (the `point` pose, bow drawn; the telegraph is a glint) | won't leave its post; flees in melee range |\n885\t| **Red Lantern ninja** | 50 | 40 / 95 | ×1.1 / 1.7; looks up | quick `slash` 10 (wind .28), shuriken 6 ×3, dodge rolls | climbs and leaps (FlowField `climb/jump`); notices ×1.3 faster |\n886\t| **Hound** (custom quadruped) | 20 | 45 / 120 | ×.8 / 1.8 | bite 8 (wind .25) | smell, bark (noise 150), eats baits from 120 |\n887\t| **Civilian** (merchant, maid, monk, drunk, noble, servant) | 15 | 25 / 80 | ×.9 / 1.6 | none | seeing the hero or a body → scream (noise 160) and flee to the nearest guard. Harming one costs −400 |\n888\t| **Disguised Red Lantern** (M3) | 50 | as a servant | ×1.1 | becomes a ninja when within 24 of the hero or when attacked | only Ki Focus shows its red aura. A Silent Cut on it is fine; on a real servant it is a civilian harm |\n889\t\n890\tBehaviors are data: `mode: 'patrol' | 'post' | 'sleep' | 'eat' | 'chat'`. Patrol routes are lists of waypoints with\n891\twaits and look-around angles; `post` guards sweep their gaze ±60 degrees every 4 s.\n892\t\n893\t### 5.12 Bosses (`53-bosses.js`)\n894\t\n895\tShared rules:\n896\t\n897\t- A `Boss` has HP, phases at HP fractions, and a pattern script (a `game.script` generator that picks moves by distance\n898\t  and phase)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"ca3cf006-8527-48ff-96c0-c8d4d5309226","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:20.393Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Intent** (built by `PlayerInput`, `Autopilot` or a test):\n\n```js\n{ move: [x, y]  /* world ground dir, length 0..1 */, walk, sprint, crouchPressed, jumpPressed, attackPressed,\n  blockDown, interactPressed, interactDown, grapplePressed, grappleDown, grappleReleased, usePressed, focusDown,\n  toolDelta, toolSlot, healPressed, lurePressed, aimPoint /* {x,y} or null */ }\n```\n\n**Body:**\n\n```js\nnew E.Mover({ x, y, z, r: 5, climbAny: false, climbMax: 30, vault: 14, hopMax: 48, staminaMax: 100,\n              run: T('heroRun'), sneak: T('heroSneak'), sprintSpeed: T('heroSprint'), jumpSpeed: 220 })\n```\n\n`climbAny` is off on purpose: roofs need the grapple, as in the source. Fed with\n`{ move, sprint, crouch, jumpPressed }` each step. `rig.update(dt, hero.rigState({...}))`.\n\n| Mode | Speed | Noise radius (*T* `noiseRun`) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| walk (stick <55% or Focus) | 50 | 0 | |\n| run | *T* 85 (Kaede 92) | 60 (Kaede ×.8) | surface multipliers from the legend |\n| sprint (stamina 20/s) | *T* 125 (Kaede 132) | 110 | |\n| crouch (toggle) | *T* 32 | 0 (gravel 12) | `hero.chest = 8`; E.sees ×.6 built in |\n| jump / land | — | land 50 (roll at 26+ drop silences it to 20) | fall >72 hurts 15 |\n| swim (deep water) | 30 | 15 (splash) | no attacks or tools except eat; visible |\n| dive (crouch in deep water) | 24 | 0 | **unseen** (exposure 0); breath *T* 12 s, then 8 dmg/s; bubbles |\n| wall hug | 24 sideways | 0 | exposure ×.6; peek at corners |\n| drag body | 24 | 10 | can't jump, strike or use tools |\n\n- **Wall hug:** crouched and pushing into a wall face (`map.wall(hero, dir)`) for .2 s presses the back to the wall\n  (custom pose: arms flat, head turned along the wall).\n  - The stick moves along the face only.\n  - At a face end, the hero leans out: the camera pans 48 units past the corner, and Shadow Sight checks from a peek\n    eye 10 units past the corner.\n  - Push away or press ○ to leave.\n- **Roll:** block + jump + direction → `hero.dodge(dir, 34)` (invulnerable mid-roll).\n- **Drag:**\n  - △ near a dead or asleep body grabs it under the arms. The victim's rig stays `down: 1` and is dragged 14 units\n    behind, facing up. △ drops it.\n  - Dropped in deep water, it sinks (splash, removed).\n  - Dropped in grass, bamboo or a lightAt <.3 spot, it is hidden (body discovery needs exposure >.35).\n- **Falls and hazards:** Mover's `rollAt` / `hurtAt`. Out-of-map or unwalkable spots → `hero.respawn()` (−10 HP).\n- **Stats** (`def('character', …)`):\n\n  | | HP | Damage | Block | Silent Cut | Grapple pull | Noise |\n  |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n  | Sojiro | 100 | ×1.2 | 85% | .9 s | ×1.0 | ×1.0 |\n  | Kaede | 80 | ×.85, attacks ×1.25 faster | 70% | .7 s | ×1.15 | ×.8 |\n\n  The hub and Shadow Trial use equal \"trial\" stats (Sojiro's) for both looks.\n\n### 5.2 Grappling hook — kaginawa (`42-grapple.js`)\n\n- **Anchors:**\n  - The auto-found ones are wall tops of solid cells whose top is between `z+16` and `z+T('grappleMaxRise')` (96),\n    within `T('grappleRange')` (112) horizontally of the hero.\n  - The rope line from the hand (z+28) to the edge point must be clear (`map.ray`), and the landing must be standable\n    (`map.standable(edge-in by 6, top)`).\n  - Plus the level's `anchors` (tree crowns, beams).\n  - Hall walls `H` and keep tiers above the next tier are excluded, so every grapple lands somewhere sensible.\n- **Targeting:**\n  - Every .1 s, score the candidates: angle to the facing (or to the cursor / aim point) + distance.\n  - The best one within a 70-degree cone gets a subtle gold diamond, plus the prompt \"R1 Grapple\".\n  - Hold R1 to aim: time slows to .5, every anchor in range shows, and the stick or cursor picks one.\n  - Release fires. Tap fires at the highlighted anchor.\n  - In mouse mode, the anchor nearest the `map.pick` point under the cursor wins.\n- **Action** `E.ACTIONS.grapple`, with beats `[['throw', .16], ['pull', dist / T('grappleSpeed')], ['mantle', .2]]`:\n  - throw: the `throw` move. The rope is drawn from `rig.hand('R')` out to the hook along a sagging curve.\n  - pull: the body moves along a quadratic Bezier from the start to the edge point with a 10-unit arc. The rig is\n    `air: true` with hands up.\n  - mantle: a hang-to-crouch pull-up onto the top, ending crouched.\n  - Noise 30 at the hook. It can be fired mid-jump. Cooldown .3 s.\n- **Rope drawing:** `r.queue` a 1-px line through 8 points (rope color `#c8b080`, shadowed), with a hook glint at the\n  anchor.\n\n### 5.3 Light, shadow and cover (`30-world.js` + `50-perception.js`)\n\n- **Light map:** a grid of half-cells (8 units), baked in a boot step per level:\n\n  ```text\n  L = ambientMoon + Σ i · (1 − d/r)² · LOS(light → point)     (LOS = map.los; clamp 0..1)\n  ```\n\n  ambientMoon is `.22` at night, `.45` at dusk, `.18` in rain and `.3` at the festival.\n- **Dynamic lights**, added at query time: guards' hand lanterns (r 48, i .8), fire, burning fire pots, and lightning\n  flashes (rain: all exposure ×2 for .25 s; the thunder sfx follows).\n- **Exposure** given to `E.sees` as `hero.exposure`:\n\n  ```text\n  lightF = lerp(1 − T('darkness'), 1, L)\n  coverF = 1 | grass/bamboo (.15 crouched / .6 standing) | dive 0 | wall hug .6 | Kakuremino .15\n  motionF = still .75 | walk 1 | run 1.15 | sprint 1.3\n  exposure = lightF · coverF · motionF · (crouch ? T('crouchVis') / .6 : 1)\n  ```\n\n  The last factor turns the engine's built-in .6 for crouching into the slider value.\n- **Visuals match gameplay:** every light in `lights` is also a `game.lights.add` (with flicker) and a prop.\n  - Ambient: `game.lights.ambient` = .38 (night), plus a cool tint.\n  - GPU lighting when available: `game.enableGPU({ map })`, which also gives wall shadows. Set both ambients so the\n    canvas fallback matches.\n- Dev overlay \"Light map\" draws L as a dithered heat map on the ground.\n\n### 5.4 Perception and guard minds (`50-perception.js`, `51-guard-brain.js`)\n\n- **Sight**, every step per awake guard:\n\n  ```js\n  E.sees(g, hero, { map, range: T('sightRange') * g.sightMul, fov: T('sightFov'), eye })\n  ```\n\n  then exposure as above, and two gates:\n  - **Look-up limit:** if the hero is >16 above the guard's eyes and the elevation angle is above `T('lookUp')`\n    (35 degrees), the guard can't see. Archers and ninja ignore this.\n  - **Smoke:** if the sight segment passes within a cloud's radius, not seen.\n- **Mind:**\n\n  ```js\n  g.mind = new E.Suspicion({ rise: T('suspRise'), decay: T('suspDecay'), forget: 7 })\n  ```\n\n  Its states are calm, notice (turn toward `mind.last`, bark), search (walk to last, look around 4 s, then a widening\n  search around it) and alert (chase or fight).\n  - Added game states: `post`, `sleep`, `eat` (bait), `chat` (pairs face each other and bark), `stunned`, `blinded`\n    (smoke), `poisoned`, `flee` (civilians, and archers with no arrow line), `returning`.\n- **Hearing:**\n\n  ```js\n  B.noise(x, y, z, loud, kind)\n  for each guard: s = E.hears(g, noise, map) * T('hearing')\n  if (s > .15) g.mind.hear(s, noise)\n  ```\n\n  Sleeping guards wake at s > .5. Hounds hear ×1.5.\n- **Smell** (hounds): within 60 (crouched 40) of the hero → bark (noise 150) and notice. Diving cancels it.\n  Fragrant baits within 120 attract them.\n- **Bodies:**\n  - A guard whose cone sees a body (`E.sees` on the body with exposure from light and cover; bodies in grass, dark or\n    water don't count) within `T('bodyRange')` (96) runs to it.\n  - It shouts (\"Assassin!\") → alert-shout noise. The level becomes **Heightened** for 90 s: sight range ×1.2, rise\n    ×1.3, and the guard runs for the bell.\n- **Barks:** each state change (and calm idles every 12–25 s) picks a line from `Story.barks[category]`. It is spoken by\n  the voice synth with a world-positioned subtitle bubble (canvas, 1.5–2.5 s), at most one bark per 2 s within the\n  screen.\n- **Guard update order:** perceive → mind → behavior → move (`g.flow` = shared FlowField cache by goal cell, LRU 24,\n  built on the **nav map**, which blocks water; ninja fields use `{ climb: 56, drop: 56, jump: 60 }`) → rig.\n\n### 5.5 Shadow Sight, the Ki Gauge and Ki Focus (`50-perception.js`, `70-hud.js`)\n\n- **Shadow Sight** (20 Hz): a guard is *visible* if `map.sight(heroEye, guard)` is true within 200 units (360 degrees;\n  from the peek eye while hugging).\n  - Otherwise, if within `T('kiRange')` (160), it is *sensed*: drawn as a translucent indigo silhouette\n    (`alpha .35, flash '#5a5aff', flashMix 1`, no shadow, no cone), but its awareness mark still shows.\n  - Otherwise it is *hidden* and not drawn.\n  - Civilians follow the same rule. The setting \"Show all enemies\" and the dev \"Reveal all\" disable it.\n- **Ki number:** `K = max over sensed or visible guards of round(99 · (1 − d / kiRange))`.\n  - The color is the highest awareness among them: calm teal `#5ad8c8`, notice yellow `#f0d050`, search orange\n    `#f09040`, alert red `#ff4a3a`.\n  - The glyph is `?` or `!`.\n  - At K ≥ 50, a soft taiko heartbeat (rate 0.8–2.2 Hz by K). Setting: Ki heartbeat.\n- **Ki Focus** (hold L2/Tab):\n  - The hero walks at most; the zoom eases to .9×; the sense radius is 220; sensed guards brighten and show their sight\n    cones through walls.\n  - Disguised Red Lanterns get a red aura (only way to spot them). Anchors and pickups in range glint. The world\n    desaturates 30%.\n  - No cost but speed.\n\n### 5.6 Alarm, reinforcements, Heightened\n\n- An alert guard shouts: noise `T('alertShout')` (160), so guards who hear it search toward the hero's position.\n- If a bell is within 240 nav units, the shouting guard (or the first to find a body) **runs to the bell**. After 1.5 s\n  of ringing (a big bronze sfx, screen toast \"The alarm bell rings!\"):\n  - all guards go to search at the hero's last known position;\n  - the level is Heightened for the rest of the mission;\n  - after `T('reinforceDelay')` (15 s), 2 reinforcements (one samurai, one ashigaru, of the level's faction) come out\n    of the nearest barracks door.\n  - At most 2 waves per mission.\n  - Killing the runner before the ring stops it (bonus line: \"The bell stays silent.\").\n- **Music:** tension layer at any notice or K ≥ 60; alert layers (taiko + fue) on any alert, faded out 4 s after the\n  last alert ends (`audio.layer`).\n- **Calm-down:** an alert guard that loses the hero for `forget` seconds searches, then returns to its route with a\n  \"lost\" bark (\"…Must have been the wind.\"). A Heightened level never fully relaxes.\n\n### 5.7 Silent Cuts — 静斬 (`41-silentcut.js`)\n\nChecked every step for the best candidate. The prompt is \"□ Silent Cut — <kind>\", and the button runs it. Only\nnon-boss enemies, and never while they are alert or in combat. `rel` is the angle between the guard's facing and the\ndirection hero→guard (0 = the hero is directly behind):\n\n| Kind | Condition | Victim | Noise |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Back** | d ≤ *T* `killRange` 18, same level (10), rel < *T* `killBackAngle` 60° | calm, notice or search, not seeing the hero this step | 0 |\n| **Side** | d ≤ 18, same level, 60° ≤ rel < 120° | calm only, not seeing the hero | 15 (grunt) |\n| **Front** | d ≤ 18, same level, rel ≥ 120° | incapacitated: asleep, eating, stunned, blinded, poisoned | 15 |\n| **From above** | hero on a top ≥14 above, horizontal d ≤ 44, `map.arcClear`, hero on ground | calm, notice or search | 0 |\n| **Undertow** (from water) | hero swimming or diving, d ≤ 20, victim on a cell next to deep water | not alert | 10 (splash) |\n\n- Each kind is an `E.ACTIONS` paired action per character (copy the engine's `takedown` structure: `beats`, `setup`,\n  `at` returning `{ x, y, z, state, other }`), built from `E.move(...)` poses and joint post-processing.\n\n  | Kind | Sojiro | Kaede |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Back | `[['grab',.16],['strike',.24],['hold',.25],['drop',.4],['recover',.18]]`: left hand over the mouth (post-processed arm), `thrust` through | a hop, then two `thrust` beats (main and offhand), `drop` |\n  | Side | a dash past with `slash` | a `spin` |\n  | Front | a `rising` cut, the victim falls backward | an `X` cut, both blades |\n  | Above | the engine's aerial leap with `overhead` | a `plunge` |\n  | Undertow | rises with a `claw`-like grab and drags the victim into the water (victim slides, sinks, splash, fades) | same |\n\n  Victims get `hurt`, `expr: 'wince'`, then `down`.\n- **Presentation:**\n  - Freeze .05.\n  - Camera zoom 1.8× and slow motion `T('slowmo')` for .55 s; letterbox.\n  - The **静斬** splash: two 32×32 brush-kanji string sprites, red `#d02a20` with a dark edge, drawn scaled ×2 at the\n    screen's center-left, with an ink-splatter burst. A small \"SILENT CUT\" caption under it.\n  - A shamisen twang + reverse-swell sting; ink-splatter decals (Blood setting).\n  - Restore after .9 s.\n- **Effects:** `bus.emit('silentCut', { kind, victim })` gives score +150; the HUD counter goes up; hub progress\n  updates.\n\n### 5.8 Combat (`43-combat.js`)\n\n- **Damage pipeline:** `B.damage(src, dst, amount, { kind, angle })` applies:\n  1. multipliers: the character's damage multiplier for hero hits; difficulty × *T* `enemyDmg` for hits on the hero;\n     *T* `enemyHp` scales enemy HP at spawn;\n  2. block (front 120 degrees, reduces by the character's block %);\n  3. i-frames (.4 s after a hit);\n  4. death → `kill` or `heroDeath` events.\n\n  Hit feedback has **no damage numbers** (the source shows none). Check `game.hitFx`'s options for turning its number\n  off; if it can't, call `game.freeze(.05)`, `game.shake`, `particles.impact`, `particles.sparks` and the hit sfx\n  yourself, plus ink drops.\n- **Hero melee:**\n  - Sojiro: `new E.Combo(['slash','backslash','overhead'], { window: .3 })`, damage 14 / 14 / 24.\n  - Kaede: `['thrust','backslash','spin']`, damage 9 / 9 / 18, at speed ×1.25.\n  - Jump attack: `plunge`, 20 / 16.\n  - `attack.hits(enemies, e => E.inArc(hero, facing, e, 20, 1.3, 10), …)`. Face the cursor in mouse mode, or the\n    nearest enemy within 40 (auto-aim).\n- **Block (L1 hold):** pose `block`. The guard's chip goes through at 15%.\n- **Parry:** press block within `T('parryWindow')` (.18 s) before an enemy swing's active beat (the last part of its\n  wind-up).\n  - The enemy is staggered 1.3 s (\"staggered\" stars).\n  - The prompt \"□ Riposte\" kills ashigaru, samurai and ninja instantly (a short cinematic, counted as a kill, not a\n    Silent Cut) and does 60 damage to bosses.\n  - A white flash, ring sfx and sparks.\n- **Enemy swings:** `E.Attack(move, { wind: base × T('enemyWindup'), … })` with visible wind-ups, longer than the\n  hero's. Red `groundArc` decals warn for area attacks.\n- **Hero HP 0:** the `die` pose, then the game over overlay. Retry restores the last checkpoint (section 5.14).\n\n### 5.9 Tools and the Bento (`44-tools.js`)\n\nThe bento has 8 compartments (2 tiers × 4). Each holds one tool type, up to that tool's stack; the same tool may fill\nseveral compartments. Stock is unlimited: what limits you is packing. The default loadout comes from the mission's\n`loadoutHint`, and the last one is remembered.\n\n| Tool | Stack | Use | Effect (numbers are TUNE entries) | Unlock |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Rice Ball** (onigiri) | 3 | eat (.6 s, vulnerable) | +40 HP | start |\n| **Poison Rice Ball** | 2 | drop at the feet or a short toss ≤48 | a guard or hound that sees it within *T* `baitRange` 80 (hounds smell 120) and is calm walks to it (`eat` state, back to the room), eats 2 s, then dies 3 s later (\"Ugh… my stomach…\"). Counts as a kill: +100 \"clean\" | start |\n| **Sleep Dango** | 2 | same as poison | the eater sleeps 25 s (snores, noise 20). Front Silent Cut allowed | rank ≥ Ekiben in \"Rice and Ash\" |\n| **Sour Plum** (umeboshi) | 3 | eat (instant) | stamina full + **soft steps** 20 s (run noise 0, sprint 30) | rank ≥ Ekiben in the Trial |\n| **Shuriken** | 10 | throw (`E.Bullets` ground plane, 300 u/s, range 160) | 8 damage; a calm guard hit turns to search toward the thrower's line | start |\n| **Smoke Bomb** | 2 | lob ≤96 (or at the feet with block held) | a cloud r 40 for *T* `smokeTime` 6 s blocks sight through it. Guards inside are `blinded` (cough, 1.5 s) and lose the hero (`mind.level` capped at search; last position stale). Big `particles.smoke` | start |\n| **Caltrops** | 2 | drop | area r 24 for 20 s: an enemy stepping in takes 6 damage, a 2 s stun, then limps (×.5 speed, 6 s). The hero is immune | start |\n| **Firecracker** | 3 | lob ≤128 | pops .8 s after landing: noise 140 at the landing, so non-alert guards search there; hounds bark | start |\n| **Fire Pot** (horokudama) | 1 | lob ≤112, explodes on impact | r 32, 45 damage (the hero too if inside), noise 220 (wakes and alerts), fire particles + light 1 s | rank ≥ Makunouchi in \"Kiri Lake\" |\n| **Straw Cloak** (kakuremino) | 1 | self | 15 s: sight rise ×.15 unless within 16, striking or sprinting; drawn as a straw-cloaked silhouette | Grand Kaiseki in any mission |\n\n- **Aiming:** thrown and lobbed tools target `intent.aimPoint` (the mouse ground point). Otherwise auto-aim at the\n  nearest visible guard in a 45-degree cone within range, else 80 units ahead. Lobs use `E.arc(from, to, 700, { apex:\n  24 })` on a small `E.Body` with a trail.\n- Each use emits `toolUsed` (results line \"Tools used\"). Pickups in levels add to the current stacks, up to the stack.\n\n### 5.10 Bodies\n\n- Dead and asleep guards stay where they fell (rig `down: 1`). Discovery is covered in section 5.4; dragging and\n  hiding in section 5.1.\n- Bodies in deep water sink. A poisoned guard's body counts as found like any other.\n- The dev overlay marks bodies and whether each is hidden.\n\n### 5.11 Enemies and civilians (`52-enemies.js`; rigs in section 6.1)\n\n| Type | HP | Speeds walk/run | Sight range / fov | Moves | Special |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Ashigaru** (spear) | 40 | 30 / 70 | ×1.0 / 1.5 | `thrust` 12 (wind .42), `overhead` butt 10 | often carries a hand lantern (lights itself: easy to see, sees well) |\n| **Samurai** (katana, sashimono) | 70 | 32 / 75 | ×1.05 / 1.5 | `slash` 16 (wind .36), `overhead` 22 (wind .5), blocks frontal hits 50% | parry target; the bell-runner of choice |\n| **Archer** (bow, on towers and roofs) | 30 | 28 / 65 | ×1.25 / 1.3; looks up | arrows 14 dmg, 260 u/s at chest height, 1.6 s draw (the `point` pose, bow drawn; the telegraph is a glint) | won't leave its post; flees in melee range |\n| **Red Lantern ninja** | 50 | 40 / 95 | ×1.1 / 1.7; looks up | quick `slash` 10 (wind .28), shuriken 6 ×3, dodge rolls | climbs and leaps (FlowField `climb/jump`); notices ×1.3 faster |\n| **Hound** (custom quadruped) | 20 | 45 / 120 | ×.8 / 1.8 | bite 8 (wind .25) | smell, bark (noise 150), eats baits from 120 |\n| **Civilian** (merchant, maid, monk, drunk, noble, servant) | 15 | 25 / 80 | ×.9 / 1.6 | none | seeing the hero or a body → scream (noise 160) and flee to the nearest guard. Harming one costs −400 |\n| **Disguised Red Lantern** (M3) | 50 | as a servant | ×1.1 | becomes a ninja when within 24 of the hero or when attacked | only Ki Focus shows its red aura. A Silent Cut on it is fine; on a real servant it is a civilian harm |\n\nBehaviors are data: `mode: 'patrol' | 'post' | 'sleep' | 'eat' | 'chat'`. Patrol routes are lists of waypoints with\nwaits and look-around angles; `post` guards sweep their gaze ±60 degrees every 4 s.\n\n### 5.12 Bosses (`53-bosses.js`)\n\nShared rules:\n\n- A `Boss` has HP, phases at HP fractions, and a pattern script (a `game.script` generator that picks moves by distance\n  and phase).","numLines":300,"startLine":599,"totalLines":1883}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YF5xujt8zJ9H2kNLMT8Fke","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
