{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2HWWaM8VYuGD3vxEW1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P8zPAjZiY4NJjEFx8q3jUT","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":1197,"limit":230},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10272,"cache_read_input_tokens":489765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10272},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"6f64d4f0-4f0a-46c8-af17-f03e7957f963","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:34.936Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2HWFCvqUKnjKSUwWFT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01P8zPAjZiY4NJjEFx8q3jUT":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":1197,"limit":230}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P8zPAjZiY4NJjEFx8q3jUT","type":"tool_result","content":"1197\tL1/R1 (keyboard: PageUp/PageDown, mouse: the \"◀ Prev page\" / \"Next page ▶\" buttons at the bottom of each page) switch\n1198\tpages; left/right stay on the focused slider. Toggles and actions are Shell buttons whose labels show their state\n1199\t(\"God mode: On\").\n1200\t\n1201\t1. **Cheats:**\n1202\t   - Toggles: God mode, Invisible to guards, No-clip (walk through walls; jump/crouch fly up/down), Infinite tools,\n1203\t     One-hit kills, Freeze AI, Reveal all enemies.\n1204\t   - Actions: Heal, Give all tools, Unlock everything.\n1205\t2. **Mission:** Complete current objective, Kill all enemies, Alert all, Calm all, Spawn guard here (cycles the type),\n1206\t   Skip to boss, Win mission (choose rank), Fail mission, Restart mission, Jump to mission…, **Edit this level**\n1207\t   (opens the Workshop on the current level).\n1208\t3. **Teleport:** to start / next objective / boss arena / exit / each zone; **to cursor** (closes the menu; the next\n1209\t   click or ✕ on the ground teleports there).\n1210\t4. **Debug view:** AI overlay (cones for all guards, state labels, suspicion bars, last-known points, patrol routes,\n1211\t   noise rings, FlowField arrows), Light map, Nav map, Hide spots, Grapple anchors, Ranges (kill range, block arc,\n1212\t   bait radius), Time scale (.25 / .5 / 1 / 2 / 4), Show frame rate (engine setting), Free camera (`cam.free`).\n1213\t5. **Balance pages**, live sliders bound to `game.settings` group `'Dev'`, each with **Reset page**, plus **Reset all\n1214\t   to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`). The 32 sliders:\n1215\t\n1216\t   **Hero**\n1217\t\n1218\t   | Key | Default | Range |\n1219\t   |---|---|---|\n1220\t   | heroRun | 85 | 60–130 |\n1221\t   | heroSneak | 32 | 18–50 |\n1222\t   | heroSprint | 125 | 90–170 |\n1223\t   | heroHpMul | 1 | .5–2 |\n1224\t   | grappleRange | 112 | 64–200 |\n1225\t   | grappleSpeed | 240 | 120–400 |\n1226\t   | breath | 12 s | 5–30 |\n1227\t   | noiseRun | 60 | 20–140 |\n1228\t\n1229\t   **Guards**\n1230\t\n1231\t   | Key | Default | Range |\n1232\t   |---|---|---|\n1233\t   | sightRange | 112 | 60–200 |\n1234\t   | sightFov | 1.5 | .8–2.4 |\n1235\t   | suspRise | 1.4 | .4–3 |\n1236\t   | suspDecay | .3 | .05–1 |\n1237\t   | darkness | .65 | 0–1 |\n1238\t   | crouchVis | .55 | .2–1 |\n1239\t   | hearing | 1 | .3–2 |\n1240\t   | lookUp | 35° | 15–70 |\n1241\t\n1242\t   **Combat and tools**\n1243\t\n1244\t   | Key | Default | Range |\n1245\t   |---|---|---|\n1246\t   | killRange | 18 | 10–30 |\n1247\t   | killBackAngle | 60° | 30–90 |\n1248\t   | parryWindow | .18 | .05–.4 |\n1249\t   | enemyDmg | 1 | .25–2 |\n1250\t   | enemyHp | 1 | .5–2 |\n1251\t   | enemyWindup | 1 | .6–1.6 |\n1252\t   | smokeTime | 6 | 2–12 |\n1253\t   | baitRange | 80 | 40–160 |\n1254\t\n1255\t   **World**\n1256\t\n1257\t   | Key | Default | Range |\n1258\t   |---|---|---|\n1259\t   | kiRange | 160 | 80–300 |\n1260\t   | alertShout | 160 | 0–320 |\n1261\t   | bodyRange | 96 | 40–180 |\n1262\t   | reinforceDelay | 15 | 5–40 |\n1263\t   | ambientNight | .38 | .15–.7 |\n1264\t   | lanternRadius | ×1 | .5–1.6 |\n1265\t   | parTimeMul | 1 | .5–2 |\n1266\t   | slowmo | .3 | .1–1 |\n1267\t\n1268\t   `B.T(key)` reads the live value (with the difficulty multiplier where noted), so a change applies on the next step.\n1269\t   Systems that cache (the light map) rebake on change.\n1270\t- The backquote key toggles the AI overlay while dev mode has been opened once this session.\n1271\t\n1272\t### 5.21 Mission Editor — \"Workshop\" (`75-workshop.js`)\n1273\t\n1274\tTenchu 2's signature feature, and the designer tool the TASK asks for: it edits the exact level JSON the campaign uses\n1275\t(section 3.6).\n1276\t\n1277\t- **Entry:** Title → Workshop (3 save slots + \"New from template\": blank 40×40, or a copy of any campaign level), or\n1278\t  Dev Mode → Edit this level.\n1279\t- **View:** the level drawn by the same renderer (lights included), a grid overlay, a cursor box drawn at the cell's\n1280\t  top height, the camera rotatable and zoomable.\n1281\t- **Panels (10-foot):**\n1282\t  - Category tabs at the top: Ground · Walls · Buildings · Props · Lights · Actors · Routes · Items · Settings.\n1283\t  - A brush strip at the bottom (big icons, the name of the focused one).\n1284\t  - The cursor cell info at top left; the control legend with glyphs at bottom right.\n1285\t- **Controls:**\n1286\t\n1287\t  | Input | Edits |\n1288\t  |---|---|\n1289\t  | **Pad** | left stick moves the cursor (repeat), right stick pans, L1/R1 change category, L2/R2 change brush, ✕ paints or places, ○ erases, □ eyedropper (pick or select), △ rotates the facing, Create test-plays, Options opens the menu |\n1290\t  | **Mouse/keys** | hover moves the cursor, left click paints (drag paints lines), right click erases, middle drag pans, wheel changes brush, Tab changes category, 1–9 pick a brush, Q/E rotate, F5 test-plays, Esc opens the menu |\n1291\t\n1292\t- **Brushes:**\n1293\t  - Ground: the 10 floor types.\n1294\t  - Walls: `#`, `W`, `F`, `H` with `d`.\n1295\t  - Buildings: `A B C D S T G K M P R`.\n1296\t  - Props: all of section 5.18's shapes.\n1297\t  - Lights: stone or paper lantern, torch, brazier.\n1298\t  - Actors: hero start, exit, target, ashigaru, samurai, archer, ninja, hound, civilian types, disguised, bosses\n1299\t    (Gonroku, Hotaru, Kurogane), bell, barracks.\n1300\t  - Routes: select a guard (□), then ✕ adds a waypoint, ○ removes the last, △ cycles the wait (0 / 1 / 2 / 4 s).\n1301\t  - Items: tool pickups, the scroll (optional objective).\n1302\t- **Settings:** name, size (32 / 40 / 48), time (dusk / night / rain / festival), par time, music.\n1303\t  - Objectives are generated: \"Silence the target\" (when a target is placed) + \"Escape\" (exit) + \"Steal the scroll\"\n1304\t    (optional, if placed). A boss placed means \"Defeat <boss>\" before the exit.\n1305\t- **Validation** before test or save: a hero start, an exit and a target or boss are present, and both are reachable\n1306\t  from the start (FlowField on the hero's map with climb 30 + grapple edges). Problems are listed in plain words and\n1307\t  the cursor jumps to them.\n1308\t- **Menu:** Test play (mission scene, mode `workshop`; results then back to the editor), Save to slot 1–3, Load,\n1309\t  Export (copies the JSON with `navigator.clipboard`, falling back to a read-only `<textarea>` overlay to select from),\n1310\t  Import (a `<textarea>` overlay; validated), Play (a fresh run with results), Exit. No `alert`, `prompt` or `confirm`:\n1311\t  questions are Shell screens.\n1312\t- **Storage:** `E.store.set('bentou:workshop:<slot>', levelJson)` / `E.store.get(...)`.\n1313\t\n1314\t### 5.22 Multiplayer — AI Hub ghost mode, and the Shadow Trial on its own (`82-hub.js`)\n1315\t\n1316\t- **Mode: `ghost`, seats `[1, 4]`.** Each player runs the same round, \"Night Delivery\" (section 6.5), in their own copy.\n1317\t  The other players appear as translucent shadow ninja in their seat colors (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n1318\t  `#f5b700`) wherever they are. They never affect the world.\n1319\t- **Boot in a session:**\n1320\t  1. Check `AIHub.active` first. If true: no title, no attract, no menus.\n1321\t  2. Go straight to the scene `hubCard`, then call\n1322\t     `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`.\n1323\t  3. If it resolves `null`, fall back to the normal title.\n1324\t  4. Otherwise build the trial level and call `AIHub.ready()` with no key press.\n1325\t- **The game's own card** (`hubCard`, canvas):\n1326\t  - The title art's rooftop at night, with up to 4 ninja lined up in seat colors (Sojiro's rig for even ids, Kaede's\n1327\t    for odd ids; equal stats).\n1328\t  - Names in a DOM overlay via `textContent` only (never HTML).\n1329\t  - Ready ticks from `card.ready`, the goal line, this player's controls as glyphs, and the countdown from `card.left`\n1330\t    (\"Paused: more time asked\" when `paused`, \"Starting…\" when `starting`).\n1331\t  - **Enter / ✕ → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ / M → `AIHub.answer('more')`** (pressing it again takes it back; name the\n1332\t    key M on the card).\n1333\t  - No menus or choices. The card draws no `Math.random` numbers: no particles or sfx variance; use\n1334\t    `AIHub.rng('card')` for cosmetic motion.\n1335\t- **Start:**\n1336\t  - On `start`, show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()` (negative) in large brush digits.\n1337\t  - Gameplay begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n1338\t  - The round clock is `AIHub.time()`; the trial's par is 300 s.\n1339\t- **Ghost traffic:**\n1340\t  - Every 100 ms, send `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: 'delivery', x, y, z, f, s, k }, { reliable: false })`, where `s` is a\n1341\t    state code (0 run, 1 crouch, 2 swim, 3 dive, 4 attack, 5 cut, 6 dead, 7 done) and `k` is kills.\n1342\t  - On finish or death, send `{ t: 'done', score }` (reliable).\n1343\t  - Receivers interpolate (`k = 1 − .002^dt`) and draw a rig at alpha .45 with an afterimage trail (`ghost` option),\n1344\t    the seat-color scarf, and a DOM name label. They are drawn only when in the same area (`a`; the whole Night\n1345\t    Delivery level is one area, `'delivery'`).\n1346\t  - `leave` removes that ghost.\n1347\t- **Progress:** `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` **every second from the start of play** (even at score 0) until the\n1348\t  result. Labels: \"Cuts 2 · Unseen\", \"Target down\", \"Escaped 3:12\".\n1349\t- **Result:**\n1350\t  - On escape or death: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats are at most 6 entries:\n1351\t    `{ 'Silent cuts': n, 'Detected': m, 'Time': '3:12', 'Rank': 'Ekiben' }`.\n1352\t  - Awards (at most 3; titles ≤24 characters, details ≤40):\n1353\t    - \"Ghost of the Moon\" (never detected);\n1354\t    - \"Silent Blade\" (5+ cuts);\n1355\t    - \"Fed by All\" (no kills except the target).\n1356\t  - **On `time-up`:** report the current score at once (well within `graceMs`).\n1357\t- **Scoring in the round:**\n1358\t  - +2000 target silenced; +1000 escaped after the target.\n1359\t  - +250 per Silent Cut; +50 per other kill.\n1360\t  - +600 if never detected, else −150 per detection.\n1361\t  - −500 per civilian harmed.\n1362\t  - Time bonus on escape: +4 per second under 300, at most 1200.\n1363\t  - Death ends the run with the score so far.\n1364\t- **On `end`:** stop all input (ignore actions) and sound (`audio.stopMusic`, mute sfx). Show a \"Round over\"\n1365\t  overlay with the standings by name (DOM `textContent`). Send nothing more.\n1366\t- **Session rules:**\n1367\t  - The pause menu shows only Resume / Settings / Controls, and Quit is off. Create the game with\n1368\t    `menu: { quit: (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? false : 'title', items: () => B.pauseItems() }`. If `connect()`\n1369\t    resolves `null`, set `game.o.menu.quit = 'title'`; the Shell reads `menu.quit` and the items function each time\n1370\t    the pause screen renders.\n1371\t  - No dev mode, Workshop, saves or attract.\n1372\t  - Create (Pad8) does nothing in a session (no objectives panel), and patch #9 ignores Options while Create is held:\n1373\t    the hub owns that pair.\n1374\t  - No other network; no `alert` / `confirm` / `prompt` / `window.open`.\n1375\t  - If the canvas can't start, `AIHub.fail('…')`.\n1376\t- **The game on its own (standalone twin): Shadow Trial.**\n1377\t  - Title → Shadow Trial runs the same \"Night Delivery\" round with the same rules and score.\n1378\t  - Your best run's ghost (a 10 Hz track saved with the score) plays alongside you, in white.\n1379\t  - A local board of the top 5 (score, rank, character, date) shows on the results.\n1380\t  - The ghost send, draw and score code is shared with the hub path.\n1381\t\n1382\t### 5.23 About / Credits (title → About; paged)\n1383\t\n1384\t1. **About:** what the game is; \"an original game inspired by *Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins* (Acquire /\n1385\t   Activision, 2000); not affiliated\"; how to play in three lines.\n1386\t2. **Source Information:** the TASK.md fields (date, source, plan = `PLAN.md`, genre and perspective, tech with\n1387\t   versions, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage). Fill them with\n1388\t   your real values; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n1389\t3. **Testing Feedback**, 4. **Engine Feedback**, 5. **Prompt Feedback:** your answers to TASK.md's questions (written at\n1390\t   the end, the same text as in your chat reply and `exit-interview.json`).\n1391\t6. **Credits:** built by (your model); plan: PLAN.md; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge) with the\n1392\t   listed patches; AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0 (unmodified); all art, music, sound and voices generated in\n1393\t   code.\n1394\t\n1395\t---\n1396\t\n1397\t## 6. Content\n1398\t\n1399\t### 6.1 Characters and rigs (`21-rigs.js`)\n1400\t\n1401\t| Who | Rig |\n1402\t|---|---|\n1403\t| **Sojiro** (player) | `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, mask: { color: '#232a44' }, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 8, cape: { len: 4, width: 3, seg: 2 } /* scarf tail */, colors: { hair: '#232a44', cloth: '#2a3050', coat: '#2a3050', pants: '#1e2236', belt: '#b0302a', boot: '#2a2a2e', glove: '#2a2a2e', cape: '#b0302a', capeIn: '#6a1a18', metal: '#d8dce8' } })` |\n1404\t| **Kaede** (player) | `size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hair: 'ponytail' (#18141c), mask: { color: '#2a1a2a' }, outfit: 'tunic', weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 5.5, offhand: { len: 5.5 }`, cloth plum `#4a2a44`, sash and scarf teal `#2a8a8a` |\n1405\t| **Granny Oshima** | `size: 1.0, build: 'chibi', hunch: .35, outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail' (grey bun #b8b0a8)`, robe brown `#5a4030`, apron; a rice paddle as a short `staff` |\n1406\t| **Lord Mibu Takanori** | `heroic 1.2, outfit: 'robe'`, kamishimo indigo `#2a3a6a` with gold trim, topknot (`ponytail`), no weapon |\n1407\t| **Chamberlain Kurogane Dosetsu** | `bulky 1.8, armor, hat: 'kabuto' (crest #c8a040), weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 14 (nodachi)`, black `#2a2a30` with red lacing `#8a1c1c`; in the briefing a plain grey robe with no armor. Phase 2: a second rig, size 2.1, `mask: { style: 'oni', color: '#b0201a' }`, `eyeGlow: '#ff5a2a'` |\n1408\t| **Magistrate Kanemori** | `bulky 1.25, outfit: 'robe'`, rich brown and gold, `hat: 'band'` (cap), no weapon; flees and cowers |\n1409\t| **Gonroku the Iron Ox** | `bulky 1.9, hair: 'spiky', sleeves: 'none', weapon: 'club'`, tattered brown, `expr: 'angry'` |\n1410\t| **Hotaru** | `heroic 1.2, hair: 'ponytail' (#2a0a10), mask: { color: '#1a1018' }, weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 5, offhand: { len: 5 } (kama)`, crimson `#8a1a2a`, a black scarf with a red lantern emblem |\n1411\t| **Tobei** | `size: 1.1, outfit: 'tunic', hat: 'band'`, brown and green, a furoshiki bundle on his back (a short wide cape in cloth `#3a6a3a`) |\n1412\t| **Brother Ittetsu** | `bulky 1.4, hair: 'bald', outfit: 'robe', weapon: 'sword'` (wooden bokken: metal `#8a6a4a`) |\n1413\t| **Disciples Ume, Kiku, Masa** | `heroic 1.15, hood, mask`, green, blue and brown cloth; carry hand lanterns |\n1414\t| **Ashigaru** | `heroic 1.15, hat: 'jingasa', armor` (dull plate), `weapon: 'spear'`; faction cloth: Kanemori ochre `#8a6a2a`, Red Lantern `#8a2a2a`, Kokaku indigo `#2a3a6a` |\n1415\t| **Samurai** | `heroic 1.25, hat: 'kabuto', armor, sashimono: <faction>, weapon: 'sword'` |\n1416\t| **Archer** | ashigaru dress, `weapon: 'bow'` |\n1417\t| **Red Lantern ninja** | `heroic 1.2, hood (#6a1a1a), mask (#1a1418)`, black cloth `#1a1418`, red sash |\n1418\t| **Civilians** | robes in varied colors: merchants `band` hats, maids in bright patterned robes with buns, monks bald in saffron, drunks with `expr` red cheeks, nobles in rich colors at the festival, servants in grey |\n1419\t| **Hound** | custom `Hound` class: a 3D skeleton (spine of 3 points, head, 4 two-segment legs on a trot cycle, a curled tail), drawn with `px.poly` / `px.disc` through `r.w()` inside `r.actor`; Akita colors (tan `#c88a4a`, cream `#f0e0c0`); states walk, run, sniff (head down), bark (head up, mouth), eat, down |\n1420\t\n1421\tPortraits for dialog are `rig.drawPortrait` of the same rigs (masks included, via patch #3).\n1422\t\n1423\t### 6.2 Missions\n1424\t\n1425\tCoarse sketches, 1 character = 2×2 cells. Author the full `rows` from them, keeping roofs within a jump or a grapple of\n1426\teach other: roof gaps of 3–4 cells, and height steps within the grapple's rise."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"e57b31ae-e1d6-406a-9c62-02ef3e51d6c2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:34.942Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","content":"L1/R1 (keyboard: PageUp/PageDown, mouse: the \"◀ Prev page\" / \"Next page ▶\" buttons at the bottom of each page) switch\npages; left/right stay on the focused slider. Toggles and actions are Shell buttons whose labels show their state\n(\"God mode: On\").\n\n1. **Cheats:**\n   - Toggles: God mode, Invisible to guards, No-clip (walk through walls; jump/crouch fly up/down), Infinite tools,\n     One-hit kills, Freeze AI, Reveal all enemies.\n   - Actions: Heal, Give all tools, Unlock everything.\n2. **Mission:** Complete current objective, Kill all enemies, Alert all, Calm all, Spawn guard here (cycles the type),\n   Skip to boss, Win mission (choose rank), Fail mission, Restart mission, Jump to mission…, **Edit this level**\n   (opens the Workshop on the current level).\n3. **Teleport:** to start / next objective / boss arena / exit / each zone; **to cursor** (closes the menu; the next\n   click or ✕ on the ground teleports there).\n4. **Debug view:** AI overlay (cones for all guards, state labels, suspicion bars, last-known points, patrol routes,\n   noise rings, FlowField arrows), Light map, Nav map, Hide spots, Grapple anchors, Ranges (kill range, block arc,\n   bait radius), Time scale (.25 / .5 / 1 / 2 / 4), Show frame rate (engine setting), Free camera (`cam.free`).\n5. **Balance pages**, live sliders bound to `game.settings` group `'Dev'`, each with **Reset page**, plus **Reset all\n   to defaults** (`game.settings.reset('Dev')`). The 32 sliders:\n\n   **Hero**\n\n   | Key | Default | Range |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | heroRun | 85 | 60–130 |\n   | heroSneak | 32 | 18–50 |\n   | heroSprint | 125 | 90–170 |\n   | heroHpMul | 1 | .5–2 |\n   | grappleRange | 112 | 64–200 |\n   | grappleSpeed | 240 | 120–400 |\n   | breath | 12 s | 5–30 |\n   | noiseRun | 60 | 20–140 |\n\n   **Guards**\n\n   | Key | Default | Range |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | sightRange | 112 | 60–200 |\n   | sightFov | 1.5 | .8–2.4 |\n   | suspRise | 1.4 | .4–3 |\n   | suspDecay | .3 | .05–1 |\n   | darkness | .65 | 0–1 |\n   | crouchVis | .55 | .2–1 |\n   | hearing | 1 | .3–2 |\n   | lookUp | 35° | 15–70 |\n\n   **Combat and tools**\n\n   | Key | Default | Range |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | killRange | 18 | 10–30 |\n   | killBackAngle | 60° | 30–90 |\n   | parryWindow | .18 | .05–.4 |\n   | enemyDmg | 1 | .25–2 |\n   | enemyHp | 1 | .5–2 |\n   | enemyWindup | 1 | .6–1.6 |\n   | smokeTime | 6 | 2–12 |\n   | baitRange | 80 | 40–160 |\n\n   **World**\n\n   | Key | Default | Range |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | kiRange | 160 | 80–300 |\n   | alertShout | 160 | 0–320 |\n   | bodyRange | 96 | 40–180 |\n   | reinforceDelay | 15 | 5–40 |\n   | ambientNight | .38 | .15–.7 |\n   | lanternRadius | ×1 | .5–1.6 |\n   | parTimeMul | 1 | .5–2 |\n   | slowmo | .3 | .1–1 |\n\n   `B.T(key)` reads the live value (with the difficulty multiplier where noted), so a change applies on the next step.\n   Systems that cache (the light map) rebake on change.\n- The backquote key toggles the AI overlay while dev mode has been opened once this session.\n\n### 5.21 Mission Editor — \"Workshop\" (`75-workshop.js`)\n\nTenchu 2's signature feature, and the designer tool the TASK asks for: it edits the exact level JSON the campaign uses\n(section 3.6).\n\n- **Entry:** Title → Workshop (3 save slots + \"New from template\": blank 40×40, or a copy of any campaign level), or\n  Dev Mode → Edit this level.\n- **View:** the level drawn by the same renderer (lights included), a grid overlay, a cursor box drawn at the cell's\n  top height, the camera rotatable and zoomable.\n- **Panels (10-foot):**\n  - Category tabs at the top: Ground · Walls · Buildings · Props · Lights · Actors · Routes · Items · Settings.\n  - A brush strip at the bottom (big icons, the name of the focused one).\n  - The cursor cell info at top left; the control legend with glyphs at bottom right.\n- **Controls:**\n\n  | Input | Edits |\n  |---|---|\n  | **Pad** | left stick moves the cursor (repeat), right stick pans, L1/R1 change category, L2/R2 change brush, ✕ paints or places, ○ erases, □ eyedropper (pick or select), △ rotates the facing, Create test-plays, Options opens the menu |\n  | **Mouse/keys** | hover moves the cursor, left click paints (drag paints lines), right click erases, middle drag pans, wheel changes brush, Tab changes category, 1–9 pick a brush, Q/E rotate, F5 test-plays, Esc opens the menu |\n\n- **Brushes:**\n  - Ground: the 10 floor types.\n  - Walls: `#`, `W`, `F`, `H` with `d`.\n  - Buildings: `A B C D S T G K M P R`.\n  - Props: all of section 5.18's shapes.\n  - Lights: stone or paper lantern, torch, brazier.\n  - Actors: hero start, exit, target, ashigaru, samurai, archer, ninja, hound, civilian types, disguised, bosses\n    (Gonroku, Hotaru, Kurogane), bell, barracks.\n  - Routes: select a guard (□), then ✕ adds a waypoint, ○ removes the last, △ cycles the wait (0 / 1 / 2 / 4 s).\n  - Items: tool pickups, the scroll (optional objective).\n- **Settings:** name, size (32 / 40 / 48), time (dusk / night / rain / festival), par time, music.\n  - Objectives are generated: \"Silence the target\" (when a target is placed) + \"Escape\" (exit) + \"Steal the scroll\"\n    (optional, if placed). A boss placed means \"Defeat <boss>\" before the exit.\n- **Validation** before test or save: a hero start, an exit and a target or boss are present, and both are reachable\n  from the start (FlowField on the hero's map with climb 30 + grapple edges). Problems are listed in plain words and\n  the cursor jumps to them.\n- **Menu:** Test play (mission scene, mode `workshop`; results then back to the editor), Save to slot 1–3, Load,\n  Export (copies the JSON with `navigator.clipboard`, falling back to a read-only `<textarea>` overlay to select from),\n  Import (a `<textarea>` overlay; validated), Play (a fresh run with results), Exit. No `alert`, `prompt` or `confirm`:\n  questions are Shell screens.\n- **Storage:** `E.store.set('bentou:workshop:<slot>', levelJson)` / `E.store.get(...)`.\n\n### 5.22 Multiplayer — AI Hub ghost mode, and the Shadow Trial on its own (`82-hub.js`)\n\n- **Mode: `ghost`, seats `[1, 4]`.** Each player runs the same round, \"Night Delivery\" (section 6.5), in their own copy.\n  The other players appear as translucent shadow ninja in their seat colors (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n  `#f5b700`) wherever they are. They never affect the world.\n- **Boot in a session:**\n  1. Check `AIHub.active` first. If true: no title, no attract, no menus.\n  2. Go straight to the scene `hubCard`, then call\n     `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`.\n  3. If it resolves `null`, fall back to the normal title.\n  4. Otherwise build the trial level and call `AIHub.ready()` with no key press.\n- **The game's own card** (`hubCard`, canvas):\n  - The title art's rooftop at night, with up to 4 ninja lined up in seat colors (Sojiro's rig for even ids, Kaede's\n    for odd ids; equal stats).\n  - Names in a DOM overlay via `textContent` only (never HTML).\n  - Ready ticks from `card.ready`, the goal line, this player's controls as glyphs, and the countdown from `card.left`\n    (\"Paused: more time asked\" when `paused`, \"Starting…\" when `starting`).\n  - **Enter / ✕ → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ / M → `AIHub.answer('more')`** (pressing it again takes it back; name the\n    key M on the card).\n  - No menus or choices. The card draws no `Math.random` numbers: no particles or sfx variance; use\n    `AIHub.rng('card')` for cosmetic motion.\n- **Start:**\n  - On `start`, show a 3-2-1 countdown from `AIHub.time()` (negative) in large brush digits.\n  - Gameplay begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n  - The round clock is `AIHub.time()`; the trial's par is 300 s.\n- **Ghost traffic:**\n  - Every 100 ms, send `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', a: 'delivery', x, y, z, f, s, k }, { reliable: false })`, where `s` is a\n    state code (0 run, 1 crouch, 2 swim, 3 dive, 4 attack, 5 cut, 6 dead, 7 done) and `k` is kills.\n  - On finish or death, send `{ t: 'done', score }` (reliable).\n  - Receivers interpolate (`k = 1 − .002^dt`) and draw a rig at alpha .45 with an afterimage trail (`ghost` option),\n    the seat-color scarf, and a DOM name label. They are drawn only when in the same area (`a`; the whole Night\n    Delivery level is one area, `'delivery'`).\n  - `leave` removes that ghost.\n- **Progress:** `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` **every second from the start of play** (even at score 0) until the\n  result. Labels: \"Cuts 2 · Unseen\", \"Target down\", \"Escaped 3:12\".\n- **Result:**\n  - On escape or death: `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once. Stats are at most 6 entries:\n    `{ 'Silent cuts': n, 'Detected': m, 'Time': '3:12', 'Rank': 'Ekiben' }`.\n  - Awards (at most 3; titles ≤24 characters, details ≤40):\n    - \"Ghost of the Moon\" (never detected);\n    - \"Silent Blade\" (5+ cuts);\n    - \"Fed by All\" (no kills except the target).\n  - **On `time-up`:** report the current score at once (well within `graceMs`).\n- **Scoring in the round:**\n  - +2000 target silenced; +1000 escaped after the target.\n  - +250 per Silent Cut; +50 per other kill.\n  - +600 if never detected, else −150 per detection.\n  - −500 per civilian harmed.\n  - Time bonus on escape: +4 per second under 300, at most 1200.\n  - Death ends the run with the score so far.\n- **On `end`:** stop all input (ignore actions) and sound (`audio.stopMusic`, mute sfx). Show a \"Round over\"\n  overlay with the standings by name (DOM `textContent`). Send nothing more.\n- **Session rules:**\n  - The pause menu shows only Resume / Settings / Controls, and Quit is off. Create the game with\n    `menu: { quit: (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? false : 'title', items: () => B.pauseItems() }`. If `connect()`\n    resolves `null`, set `game.o.menu.quit = 'title'`; the Shell reads `menu.quit` and the items function each time\n    the pause screen renders.\n  - No dev mode, Workshop, saves or attract.\n  - Create (Pad8) does nothing in a session (no objectives panel), and patch #9 ignores Options while Create is held:\n    the hub owns that pair.\n  - No other network; no `alert` / `confirm` / `prompt` / `window.open`.\n  - If the canvas can't start, `AIHub.fail('…')`.\n- **The game on its own (standalone twin): Shadow Trial.**\n  - Title → Shadow Trial runs the same \"Night Delivery\" round with the same rules and score.\n  - Your best run's ghost (a 10 Hz track saved with the score) plays alongside you, in white.\n  - A local board of the top 5 (score, rank, character, date) shows on the results.\n  - The ghost send, draw and score code is shared with the hub path.\n\n### 5.23 About / Credits (title → About; paged)\n\n1. **About:** what the game is; \"an original game inspired by *Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins* (Acquire /\n   Activision, 2000); not affiliated\"; how to play in three lines.\n2. **Source Information:** the TASK.md fields (date, source, plan = `PLAN.md`, genre and perspective, tech with\n   versions, art direction, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage). Fill them with\n   your real values; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n3. **Testing Feedback**, 4. **Engine Feedback**, 5. **Prompt Feedback:** your answers to TASK.md's questions (written at\n   the end, the same text as in your chat reply and `exit-interview.json`).\n6. **Credits:** built by (your model); plan: PLAN.md; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge) with the\n   listed patches; AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0 (unmodified); all art, music, sound and voices generated in\n   code.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 Characters and rigs (`21-rigs.js`)\n\n| Who | Rig |\n|---|---|\n| **Sojiro** (player) | `new E.Humanoid({ size: 1.25, build: 'heroic', hood: true, mask: { color: '#232a44' }, outfit: 'coat', sleeves: 'long', weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 8, cape: { len: 4, width: 3, seg: 2 } /* scarf tail */, colors: { hair: '#232a44', cloth: '#2a3050', coat: '#2a3050', pants: '#1e2236', belt: '#b0302a', boot: '#2a2a2e', glove: '#2a2a2e', cape: '#b0302a', capeIn: '#6a1a18', metal: '#d8dce8' } })` |\n| **Kaede** (player) | `size: 1.2, build: 'heroic', hair: 'ponytail' (#18141c), mask: { color: '#2a1a2a' }, outfit: 'tunic', weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 5.5, offhand: { len: 5.5 }`, cloth plum `#4a2a44`, sash and scarf teal `#2a8a8a` |\n| **Granny Oshima** | `size: 1.0, build: 'chibi', hunch: .35, outfit: 'robe', hair: 'ponytail' (grey bun #b8b0a8)`, robe brown `#5a4030`, apron; a rice paddle as a short `staff` |\n| **Lord Mibu Takanori** | `heroic 1.2, outfit: 'robe'`, kamishimo indigo `#2a3a6a` with gold trim, topknot (`ponytail`), no weapon |\n| **Chamberlain Kurogane Dosetsu** | `bulky 1.8, armor, hat: 'kabuto' (crest #c8a040), weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 14 (nodachi)`, black `#2a2a30` with red lacing `#8a1c1c`; in the briefing a plain grey robe with no armor. Phase 2: a second rig, size 2.1, `mask: { style: 'oni', color: '#b0201a' }`, `eyeGlow: '#ff5a2a'` |\n| **Magistrate Kanemori** | `bulky 1.25, outfit: 'robe'`, rich brown and gold, `hat: 'band'` (cap), no weapon; flees and cowers |\n| **Gonroku the Iron Ox** | `bulky 1.9, hair: 'spiky', sleeves: 'none', weapon: 'club'`, tattered brown, `expr: 'angry'` |\n| **Hotaru** | `heroic 1.2, hair: 'ponytail' (#2a0a10), mask: { color: '#1a1018' }, weapon: 'sword', bladeLen: 5, offhand: { len: 5 } (kama)`, crimson `#8a1a2a`, a black scarf with a red lantern emblem |\n| **Tobei** | `size: 1.1, outfit: 'tunic', hat: 'band'`, brown and green, a furoshiki bundle on his back (a short wide cape in cloth `#3a6a3a`) |\n| **Brother Ittetsu** | `bulky 1.4, hair: 'bald', outfit: 'robe', weapon: 'sword'` (wooden bokken: metal `#8a6a4a`) |\n| **Disciples Ume, Kiku, Masa** | `heroic 1.15, hood, mask`, green, blue and brown cloth; carry hand lanterns |\n| **Ashigaru** | `heroic 1.15, hat: 'jingasa', armor` (dull plate), `weapon: 'spear'`; faction cloth: Kanemori ochre `#8a6a2a`, Red Lantern `#8a2a2a`, Kokaku indigo `#2a3a6a` |\n| **Samurai** | `heroic 1.25, hat: 'kabuto', armor, sashimono: <faction>, weapon: 'sword'` |\n| **Archer** | ashigaru dress, `weapon: 'bow'` |\n| **Red Lantern ninja** | `heroic 1.2, hood (#6a1a1a), mask (#1a1418)`, black cloth `#1a1418`, red sash |\n| **Civilians** | robes in varied colors: merchants `band` hats, maids in bright patterned robes with buns, monks bald in saffron, drunks with `expr` red cheeks, nobles in rich colors at the festival, servants in grey |\n| **Hound** | custom `Hound` class: a 3D skeleton (spine of 3 points, head, 4 two-segment legs on a trot cycle, a curled tail), drawn with `px.poly` / `px.disc` through `r.w()` inside `r.actor`; Akita colors (tan `#c88a4a`, cream `#f0e0c0`); states walk, run, sniff (head down), bark (head up, mouth), eat, down |\n\nPortraits for dialog are `rig.drawPortrait` of the same rigs (masks included, via patch #3).\n\n### 6.2 Missions\n\nCoarse sketches, 1 character = 2×2 cells. Author the full `rows` from them, keeping roofs within a jump or a grapple of\neach other: roof gaps of 3–4 cells, and height steps within the grapple's rise.","numLines":230,"startLine":1197,"totalLines":1883}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P8zPAjZiY4NJjEFx8q3jUT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
