{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2HuGo2ipnXyUA3Z5WE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SPHFypnUYUEErab9JR4AJP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":1426,"limit":170},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7845,"cache_read_input_tokens":500037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7845},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"4299289d-f476-4e9f-bd1c-060e2276cdd2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:41.108Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2HtzwG54x91eDBBU2J","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SPHFypnUYUEErab9JR4AJP":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","offset":1426,"limit":170}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPHFypnUYUEErab9JR4AJP","type":"tool_result","content":"1426\teach other: roof gaps of 3–4 cells, and height steps within the grapple's rise.\n1427\t\n1428\t#### Mission 0 — \"The Trial of the Second Tier\" (training; 40×28; dusk turning to night; petals; music `training`)\n1429\t\n1430\t```text\n1431\t####################\n1432\t#AAAAAA..FFFF\"\"\"\"\"\"\"#   A the Jubako-ya shop (h40)   F bamboo fence (vault)   \" bamboo grove\n1433\t#AAAAAA....,,\"\"\"1\"\"\"#   1 Disciple Ume (lantern, slow loop in the grove)\n1434\t#..@..........\"\"\"\"\"\"#   @ start, the back porch (Granny watches from the door)\n1435\t#..PP....W.W......C.#   P planters (cover)   W low walls h30 (climb)   C kura storehouse h48\n1436\t#..PP....W.W....CCCC#\n1437\t#.......~~~~~...CCCC#   ~ koi pond (deep): Disciple Kiku (2) stands at the bank\n1438\t#..,,,..~~~~~2..CC3C#   3 Disciple Masa below the kura's edge (the Hawk Drop target)\n1439\t#.............t..b..#   t persimmon tree (grapple anchor)   b bait test spot (training dummy guard \"Big Daikon\")\n1440\t#..:::::::::........#   : raked-gravel sparring ring (Brother Ittetsu)\n1441\t#..:::::::::...dd...#   d practice dummies (combo practice)\n1442\t####################\n1443\t```\n1444\t\n1445\tBeats, each with a canvas tutorial card and a Granny line; each teaches by doing:\n1446\t\n1447\t1. Move, run, walk with a light tilt, crouch, jump, vault the fence, climb the low wall.\n1448\t2. The Ki Gauge, hiding in bamboo, and Ume's token by a Back \"Silent Mark\". Training cuts are marks: the disciple sits\n1449\t   down, \"defeated\". The same choreography as a Silent Cut, but with a chalk-white splash and no blood.\n1450\t3. Swim and dive past Kiku; an Undertow mark.\n1451\t4. Grapple to the kura roof (and to the persimmon tree), cross, then a mark from above on Masa.\n1452\t5. Tools: throw a firecracker to pull \"Big Daikon\" off his post. Drop a Poison Rice Ball; in the Trial, Granny has\n1453\t   swapped the poison for a sleeping herb, so Big Daikon eats it and dozes off. Then a front mark. Smoke test:\n1454\t   Ittetsu's lantern-bearers spot you deliberately; smoke and slip away.\n1455\t6. Spar with Brother Ittetsu (block, parry, roll, combo).\n1456\t7. Return to Granny → results.\n1457\t\n1458\tPar 420 s. Unlocks: Sour Plum at Ekiben or better.\n1459\t\n1460\t#### Mission 1 — \"Rice and Ash\" (castle town; 56×48; night; petals; music `m1`; faction Kanemori)\n1461\t\n1462\t```text\n1463\t############################\n1464\t#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW....#   North: Kanemori's walled mansion\n1465\t#W::::::::W HHHHHHHHH  W...#   : inner gravel court = Gonroku's arena\n1466\t#W::::::::d d___K___H  W.T.#   H hall (enterable, roof cap): the feast; K Kanemori, 2 maids, 1 samurai\n1467\t#W::::::::W H_______H  W...#   T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n1468\t#WWWWWdWWWW HHHHdHHHH  W...#   d doorways\n1469\t#W ~~~ ll  ,,,   CC    W...#   ~ garden pond, l stone lanterns, C kura (the strongbox: optional ledger)\n1470\t#WWWWWWWWWWgWWWWWWWWWWWW...#   g front gate (2 gate guards); a side door on the east wall\n1471\t#....AA..BB....BB...AA.....#   Middle: market square; ! alarm bell; samurai pair patrol;\n1472\t#.AA.AA..BB.!..BB...AA.AA..#   noodle stall lights (yatai), 2 drunk civilians\n1473\t#.AA........DD.......D.DD..#\n1474\t#.BB..DD..AA....AA...BB....#   South: alleys and rooftops; 3 ashigaru, 1 hound in the rice-merchant yard\n1475\t#.BB......AA.,,.AA...BB....#\n1476\t#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   canal (deep): arrive by boat at the east end, leave by the boat (X) at the west end\n1477\t#X~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@#\n1478\t############################\n1479\t```\n1480\t\n1481\t- **Enemies:** 9 ashigaru, 4 samurai, 1 archer, 1 hound; 4 civilians (2 drunks, 2 maids).\n1482\t- **Objectives:**\n1483\t  1. Silence Magistrate Kanemori (in the feast hall).\n1484\t  2. *(optional)* Find what Kanemori hides (the strongbox in the kura: the letter with the black iron seal).\n1485\t  3. Defeat Gonroku. The fight starts on `objective:kill` or on entering the inner court, whichever comes first. The\n1486\t     hall's west door opens onto the court, the only way back out, so the fight can't be skipped.\n1487\t  4. Escape by the canal boat.\n1488\t- **Kanemori alerted:** he runs into the inner court and cowers behind Gonroku. No escape, no fail. After Gonroku falls,\n1489\t  his \"cornered\" line plays as you approach.\n1490\t- **Checkpoints:** inside the compound wall; after Gonroku.\n1491\t- Par 720 s. Unlocks: Sleep Dango at Ekiben or better.\n1492\t\n1493\t#### Mission 2 — \"The Fort at Kiri Lake\" (60×52; rain + lightning; music `m2`; faction Red Lantern)\n1494\t\n1495\t```text\n1496\t##############################\n1497\t#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~############.#   West: reed shore (,) and fishing huts (A); start @ and the escape boat X\n1498\t#,AA,,,~~~~~~~~~#T::::::::T#.#   ~ lake channel (deep, 9 cells): archers on towers T sweep it with lanterns\n1499\t#,AA,@,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:!:CC:#.#   # fort outer wall h56 (grapple); B barracks (reinforcements); ! bell\n1500\t#,,,,X,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:::CC:#.#   C storehouses; Q bamboo cage with Tobei (north-east)\n1501\t#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#::::::::Q:#.#   w water gate (closed; lever L inside opens it: the escort route)\n1502\t#,AA,,,~~~=====~w::L::::::::.#   = pier (Hotaru's arena on the escape route)\n1503\t#,AA,,,~~~=====~#:::::::::::.#\n1504\t#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#T:m=R=m=R=mT#   dock: m mooring posts (3) holding rice barges R (optional: cut them loose)\n1505\t##############################\n1506\t```\n1507\t\n1508\t- **Enemies:** 6 ashigaru, 3 samurai, 3 archers, 3 Red Lantern ninja (rooftops), 2 hounds.\n1509\t- **Objectives:**\n1510\t  1. Rescue Tobei (cage: hold △ 1.5 s to open).\n1511\t  2. Open the water gate (lever).\n1512\t  3. Escort Tobei to the boat in the reeds.\n1513\t  4. *(optional)* Cut the rice barges loose (0/3: hold △ 1.5 s at each post; the barges drift away downstream).\n1514\t  5. Defeat Hotaru (an ambush on the pier, a trigger on the escort route).\n1515\t- **Fail:** Tobei falls.\n1516\t- **Checkpoints:** inside the fort; after the rescue; after Hotaru.\n1517\t- Par 900 s. Unlocks: Fire Pot at Makunouchi or better.\n1518\t- Lightning flashes briefly expose everyone (section 5.3).\n1519\t\n1520\t#### Mission 3 — \"Moon over Kokaku\" (64×56; festival night, a huge moon; maple leaves; music `m3`; faction Kokaku + Red Lantern)\n1521\t\n1522\t```text\n1523\t################################\n1524\t#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   outer moat (deep); start @ swimming at the south\n1525\t#~##########################~~~#   # ishigaki wall h56; T corner towers (grapple anchors)\n1526\t#~#T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,T#~~#   second bailey: the festival garden; lantern strings, stalls,\n1527\t#~#,  stalls   ll   ll  ,,,,#~~#   6 nobles and servants (civilians) + 3 disguised Red Lanterns\n1528\t#~#,  HHHH(tea pavilion) ,,,#~~#   H tea pavilion (hall): the poisoned sake flask (stopTimer objective)\n1529\t#~#,  H__H   ll    ll   ,,,,#~~#\n1530\t#~#WWWWWWWWWWWdWWWWWWWWWWWWW#~~#   W inner wall h30, gate d\n1531\t#~#::::GGGGGGGG::::::::!::::#~~#   honmaru: keep tiers G h64 (16×16), K h112 (12×12), M h160 (8×8)\n1532\t#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   samurai and archers on each tier's roof walkway\n1533\t#~#::::GGKMMKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   the top of M = Kurogane's arena (shachihoko, moon behind)\n1534\t#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n1535\t#~#::::GGGGGGGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n1536\t#~##########################~~~#\n1537\t#~~~~~~~~~~@~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#\n1538\t################################\n1539\t```\n1540\t\n1541\t- **Enemies:** 6 samurai, 6 ashigaru, 4 archers, 2 Red Lantern ninja + 3 disguised, 1 hound; 6 civilians.\n1542\t- **Objectives:**\n1543\t  1. Find the poisoned sake before the moon is high (12:00 timer; swap it at the pavilion: interact 1 s).\n1544\t  2. Climb the keep.\n1545\t  3. Defeat Kurogane.\n1546\t- **Optional:** silence the 3 disguised Red Lanterns (0/3; Ki Focus shows them).\n1547\t- **Checkpoints:** inside the bailey; after the swap; at the keep's second tier; at the arena.\n1548\t- Par 960 s.\n1549\t\n1550\t### 6.3 Enemy totals by mission (for balancing)\n1551\t\n1552\t| Mission | Ashigaru | Samurai | Archers | Ninja | Hounds | Civilians | Boss |\n1553\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1554\t| Trial | — (3 disciples + 1 dummy guard) | — | — | — | — | — | Ittetsu |\n1555\t| Rice and Ash | 9 | 4 | 1 | — | 1 | 4 | Gonroku |\n1556\t| Kiri Lake | 6 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 2 | — | Hotaru |\n1557\t| Moon over Kokaku | 6 | 6 | 4 | 2 + 3 disguised | 1 | 6 | Kurogane |\n1558\t| Night Delivery (trial / hub) | 3 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | — (target: Broker Sakubei) |\n1559\t\n1560\t### 6.4 Tools: see section 5.9 (10 tools; 6 at the start, 4 unlocked by rank)\n1561\t\n1562\t### 6.5 \"Night Delivery\" — the Shadow Trial and AI Hub round (level id `delivery`; 34×30; night; music `m1`)\n1563\t\n1564\t```text\n1565\t#################\n1566\t#~~~~~~~X~~~~~~~#   canal along the north edge; X the canal gate (exit)\n1567\t#WWWWWWWdWWWWWWW#   W compound wall h30 (climb) with the canal gate d\n1568\t#W..CC....T..CCW#   C two kura h48, roofs a grapple apart; T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n1569\t#W..CC.......CCW#\n1570\t#W,,....HHH....W#   H small hall: Sakubei counting coins (target), a clerk (civilian)\n1571\t#W,,.l..H_H..l.W#   l stone lanterns (light pools); , tall grass by the wall\n1572\t#W....~~~....,,W#   ~ pond (deep: dive past the samurai's beat)\n1573\t#W..h.~~~......W#   h hound on a short beat by the storehouse\n1574\t#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWW#\n1575\t#.......@.......#   @ start outside the south wall\n1576\t#################\n1577\t```\n1578\t\n1579\t- The rice broker Sakubei's walled yard by the canal.\n1580\t- **Guards:** 3 ashigaru (one a lantern patrol on the inner loop), 2 samurai (one posted at the hall door), 1 archer,\n1581\t  1 Red Lantern ninja on the kura roofs; 1 hound; 2 civilians (clerks).\n1582\t- The objective is to silence Sakubei and escape through the canal gate. Par 300 s.\n1583\t- The level is the same for every copy: static data, no randomness at build. Patrols are deterministic with\n1584\t  `Math.random` seeded by the hub.\n1585\t\n1586\t### 6.6 Story script (tone: earnest, terse feudal drama; deadpan bento details; ASCII only)\n1587\t\n1588\t**Opening crawl** (white brush text on dark paper, Granny's voice):\n1589\t\n1590\t> The Sengoku era. Lords devour lords, and the land devours the poor.\n1591\t> In Kasugai Province the granaries are full, and the people starve.\n1592\t> In the shadow of Kokaku Castle stands a humble shop, the Jubako-ya.\n1593\t> It sells lunchboxes to the lord's household. Every box has two tiers.\n1594\t> So does the shop.\n1595\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05c1fc6a-91e2-4dc5-aada-febbecf3984e","uuid":"9c9b473f-7774-44bd-84b0-8cd3dcf9ca1c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:41.113Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174734__xb43d63/work/PLAN.md","content":"each other: roof gaps of 3–4 cells, and height steps within the grapple's rise.\n\n#### Mission 0 — \"The Trial of the Second Tier\" (training; 40×28; dusk turning to night; petals; music `training`)\n\n```text\n####################\n#AAAAAA..FFFF\"\"\"\"\"\"\"#   A the Jubako-ya shop (h40)   F bamboo fence (vault)   \" bamboo grove\n#AAAAAA....,,\"\"\"1\"\"\"#   1 Disciple Ume (lantern, slow loop in the grove)\n#..@..........\"\"\"\"\"\"#   @ start, the back porch (Granny watches from the door)\n#..PP....W.W......C.#   P planters (cover)   W low walls h30 (climb)   C kura storehouse h48\n#..PP....W.W....CCCC#\n#.......~~~~~...CCCC#   ~ koi pond (deep): Disciple Kiku (2) stands at the bank\n#..,,,..~~~~~2..CC3C#   3 Disciple Masa below the kura's edge (the Hawk Drop target)\n#.............t..b..#   t persimmon tree (grapple anchor)   b bait test spot (training dummy guard \"Big Daikon\")\n#..:::::::::........#   : raked-gravel sparring ring (Brother Ittetsu)\n#..:::::::::...dd...#   d practice dummies (combo practice)\n####################\n```\n\nBeats, each with a canvas tutorial card and a Granny line; each teaches by doing:\n\n1. Move, run, walk with a light tilt, crouch, jump, vault the fence, climb the low wall.\n2. The Ki Gauge, hiding in bamboo, and Ume's token by a Back \"Silent Mark\". Training cuts are marks: the disciple sits\n   down, \"defeated\". The same choreography as a Silent Cut, but with a chalk-white splash and no blood.\n3. Swim and dive past Kiku; an Undertow mark.\n4. Grapple to the kura roof (and to the persimmon tree), cross, then a mark from above on Masa.\n5. Tools: throw a firecracker to pull \"Big Daikon\" off his post. Drop a Poison Rice Ball; in the Trial, Granny has\n   swapped the poison for a sleeping herb, so Big Daikon eats it and dozes off. Then a front mark. Smoke test:\n   Ittetsu's lantern-bearers spot you deliberately; smoke and slip away.\n6. Spar with Brother Ittetsu (block, parry, roll, combo).\n7. Return to Granny → results.\n\nPar 420 s. Unlocks: Sour Plum at Ekiben or better.\n\n#### Mission 1 — \"Rice and Ash\" (castle town; 56×48; night; petals; music `m1`; faction Kanemori)\n\n```text\n############################\n#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWWW....#   North: Kanemori's walled mansion\n#W::::::::W HHHHHHHHH  W...#   : inner gravel court = Gonroku's arena\n#W::::::::d d___K___H  W.T.#   H hall (enterable, roof cap): the feast; K Kanemori, 2 maids, 1 samurai\n#W::::::::W H_______H  W...#   T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n#WWWWWdWWWW HHHHdHHHH  W...#   d doorways\n#W ~~~ ll  ,,,   CC    W...#   ~ garden pond, l stone lanterns, C kura (the strongbox: optional ledger)\n#WWWWWWWWWWgWWWWWWWWWWWW...#   g front gate (2 gate guards); a side door on the east wall\n#....AA..BB....BB...AA.....#   Middle: market square; ! alarm bell; samurai pair patrol;\n#.AA.AA..BB.!..BB...AA.AA..#   noodle stall lights (yatai), 2 drunk civilians\n#.AA........DD.......D.DD..#\n#.BB..DD..AA....AA...BB....#   South: alleys and rooftops; 3 ashigaru, 1 hound in the rice-merchant yard\n#.BB......AA.,,.AA...BB....#\n#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   canal (deep): arrive by boat at the east end, leave by the boat (X) at the west end\n#X~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@#\n############################\n```\n\n- **Enemies:** 9 ashigaru, 4 samurai, 1 archer, 1 hound; 4 civilians (2 drunks, 2 maids).\n- **Objectives:**\n  1. Silence Magistrate Kanemori (in the feast hall).\n  2. *(optional)* Find what Kanemori hides (the strongbox in the kura: the letter with the black iron seal).\n  3. Defeat Gonroku. The fight starts on `objective:kill` or on entering the inner court, whichever comes first. The\n     hall's west door opens onto the court, the only way back out, so the fight can't be skipped.\n  4. Escape by the canal boat.\n- **Kanemori alerted:** he runs into the inner court and cowers behind Gonroku. No escape, no fail. After Gonroku falls,\n  his \"cornered\" line plays as you approach.\n- **Checkpoints:** inside the compound wall; after Gonroku.\n- Par 720 s. Unlocks: Sleep Dango at Ekiben or better.\n\n#### Mission 2 — \"The Fort at Kiri Lake\" (60×52; rain + lightning; music `m2`; faction Red Lantern)\n\n```text\n##############################\n#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~############.#   West: reed shore (,) and fishing huts (A); start @ and the escape boat X\n#,AA,,,~~~~~~~~~#T::::::::T#.#   ~ lake channel (deep, 9 cells): archers on towers T sweep it with lanterns\n#,AA,@,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:!:CC:#.#   # fort outer wall h56 (grapple); B barracks (reinforcements); ! bell\n#,,,,X,~~~~~~~~~#:BBB:::CC:#.#   C storehouses; Q bamboo cage with Tobei (north-east)\n#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#::::::::Q:#.#   w water gate (closed; lever L inside opens it: the escort route)\n#,AA,,,~~~=====~w::L::::::::.#   = pier (Hotaru's arena on the escape route)\n#,AA,,,~~~=====~#:::::::::::.#\n#,,,,,,~~~~~~~~~#T:m=R=m=R=mT#   dock: m mooring posts (3) holding rice barges R (optional: cut them loose)\n##############################\n```\n\n- **Enemies:** 6 ashigaru, 3 samurai, 3 archers, 3 Red Lantern ninja (rooftops), 2 hounds.\n- **Objectives:**\n  1. Rescue Tobei (cage: hold △ 1.5 s to open).\n  2. Open the water gate (lever).\n  3. Escort Tobei to the boat in the reeds.\n  4. *(optional)* Cut the rice barges loose (0/3: hold △ 1.5 s at each post; the barges drift away downstream).\n  5. Defeat Hotaru (an ambush on the pier, a trigger on the escort route).\n- **Fail:** Tobei falls.\n- **Checkpoints:** inside the fort; after the rescue; after Hotaru.\n- Par 900 s. Unlocks: Fire Pot at Makunouchi or better.\n- Lightning flashes briefly expose everyone (section 5.3).\n\n#### Mission 3 — \"Moon over Kokaku\" (64×56; festival night, a huge moon; maple leaves; music `m3`; faction Kokaku + Red Lantern)\n\n```text\n################################\n#~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#   outer moat (deep); start @ swimming at the south\n#~##########################~~~#   # ishigaki wall h56; T corner towers (grapple anchors)\n#~#T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,T#~~#   second bailey: the festival garden; lantern strings, stalls,\n#~#,  stalls   ll   ll  ,,,,#~~#   6 nobles and servants (civilians) + 3 disguised Red Lanterns\n#~#,  HHHH(tea pavilion) ,,,#~~#   H tea pavilion (hall): the poisoned sake flask (stopTimer objective)\n#~#,  H__H   ll    ll   ,,,,#~~#\n#~#WWWWWWWWWWWdWWWWWWWWWWWWW#~~#   W inner wall h30, gate d\n#~#::::GGGGGGGG::::::::!::::#~~#   honmaru: keep tiers G h64 (16×16), K h112 (12×12), M h160 (8×8)\n#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   samurai and archers on each tier's roof walkway\n#~#::::GGKMMKGG:::::::::::::#~~#   the top of M = Kurogane's arena (shachihoko, moon behind)\n#~#::::GGKKKKGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n#~#::::GGGGGGGG:::::::::::::#~~#\n#~##########################~~~#\n#~~~~~~~~~~@~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~#\n################################\n```\n\n- **Enemies:** 6 samurai, 6 ashigaru, 4 archers, 2 Red Lantern ninja + 3 disguised, 1 hound; 6 civilians.\n- **Objectives:**\n  1. Find the poisoned sake before the moon is high (12:00 timer; swap it at the pavilion: interact 1 s).\n  2. Climb the keep.\n  3. Defeat Kurogane.\n- **Optional:** silence the 3 disguised Red Lanterns (0/3; Ki Focus shows them).\n- **Checkpoints:** inside the bailey; after the swap; at the keep's second tier; at the arena.\n- Par 960 s.\n\n### 6.3 Enemy totals by mission (for balancing)\n\n| Mission | Ashigaru | Samurai | Archers | Ninja | Hounds | Civilians | Boss |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Trial | — (3 disciples + 1 dummy guard) | — | — | — | — | — | Ittetsu |\n| Rice and Ash | 9 | 4 | 1 | — | 1 | 4 | Gonroku |\n| Kiri Lake | 6 | 3 | 3 | 3 | 2 | — | Hotaru |\n| Moon over Kokaku | 6 | 6 | 4 | 2 + 3 disguised | 1 | 6 | Kurogane |\n| Night Delivery (trial / hub) | 3 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 2 | — (target: Broker Sakubei) |\n\n### 6.4 Tools: see section 5.9 (10 tools; 6 at the start, 4 unlocked by rank)\n\n### 6.5 \"Night Delivery\" — the Shadow Trial and AI Hub round (level id `delivery`; 34×30; night; music `m1`)\n\n```text\n#################\n#~~~~~~~X~~~~~~~#   canal along the north edge; X the canal gate (exit)\n#WWWWWWWdWWWWWWW#   W compound wall h30 (climb) with the canal gate d\n#W..CC....T..CCW#   C two kura h48, roofs a grapple apart; T watchtower + archer (lantern)\n#W..CC.......CCW#\n#W,,....HHH....W#   H small hall: Sakubei counting coins (target), a clerk (civilian)\n#W,,.l..H_H..l.W#   l stone lanterns (light pools); , tall grass by the wall\n#W....~~~....,,W#   ~ pond (deep: dive past the samurai's beat)\n#W..h.~~~......W#   h hound on a short beat by the storehouse\n#WWWWWWWWWWWWWWW#\n#.......@.......#   @ start outside the south wall\n#################\n```\n\n- The rice broker Sakubei's walled yard by the canal.\n- **Guards:** 3 ashigaru (one a lantern patrol on the inner loop), 2 samurai (one posted at the hall door), 1 archer,\n  1 Red Lantern ninja on the kura roofs; 1 hound; 2 civilians (clerks).\n- The objective is to silence Sakubei and escape through the canal gate. Par 300 s.\n- The level is the same for every copy: static data, no randomness at build. Patrols are deterministic with\n  `Math.random` seeded by the hub.\n\n### 6.6 Story script (tone: earnest, terse feudal drama; deadpan bento details; ASCII only)\n\n**Opening crawl** (white brush text on dark paper, Granny's voice):\n\n> The Sengoku era. Lords devour lords, and the land devours the poor.\n> In Kasugai Province the granaries are full, and the people starve.\n> In the shadow of Kokaku Castle stands a humble shop, the Jubako-ya.\n> It sells lunchboxes to the lord's household. Every box has two tiers.\n> So does the shop.\n","numLines":170,"startLine":1426,"totalLines":1883}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SPHFypnUYUEErab9JR4AJP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
